ance authorization handling\n\n- Replaced direct axios calls with a centralized httpClient across various services, including authorizationService, dashboardService, and questionnaireTemplatesApi, improving consistency and maintainability.\n- Updated AuthorizationController to enforce authorization checks by re-enabling the [Authorize] attribute.\n- Streamlined the use of authentication tokens in the application, ensuring better management of user sessions and API requests.\n- Refactored widget components to utilize the new httpClient for API interactions, enhancing the overall architecture.\n\nThese changes improve the application''s structure and ensure a more cohesive approach to API communication and authorization management.","tree":{"sha":"c95891797e8468618d76f0ee0d9e5766c33631fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcocastellani/supplerPortal/git/trees/c95891797e8468618d76f0ee0d9e5766c33631fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcocastellani/supplerPortal/git/commits/3ce82ec2ff838abd4c4e857b3b897a1ee7d1301e","verification":{"payload":"tree c95891797e8468618d76f0ee0d9e5766c33631fe\nparent 9c551081aed76397b15a1adb9f234bb35182c166\nauthor Marco Castellani <marcocastellani@hotmail.com> 1751195210 +0200\ncommitter Marco Castellani <marcocastellani@hotmail.com> 1751195210 +0200\n\nrefactor: centralize HTTP client usage and enhance authorization handling\n\n- Replaced direct axios calls with a centralized httpClient across various services, including authorizationService, dashboardService, and questionnaireTemplatesApi, improving consistency and maintainability.\n- Updated AuthorizationController to enforce authorization checks by re-enabling the [Authorize] attribute.\n- Streamlined the use of authentication tokens in the application, ensuring better management of user sessions and API requests.\n- Refactored widget components to utilize the new httpClient for API interactions, enhancing the overall architecture.\n\nThese changes improve the application''s st