ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/6587857bf392d8148a034b443fdab982242fae35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:19:28Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:19:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): unblock FuzeX portal self-registration (#81)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `design-frames-service` pod carries the FuzeFront self-registration\ninit container — the thing that puts FuzeX in the FuzeFront portal menu.\nIn prod it has been `Pending` for 7d+ with `0/N nodes available: …\ndidn''t match PersistentVolume''s node affinity` on PVC\n`fuzex-fuzex-data`: a **local-path** PV pinned to a since-tainted node.\nA local-path PV binds to a single node, so once that node was tainted\nthe claim''s pod could never schedule anywhere — and never registered.\nThis is the node-local-storage-for-a-stateful-pod failure class\n(FuzeInfra#980; the same loss took three local-path PVs in\nFuzeInfra#924).\n\nThis PR moves the design-store persistence onto node-agnostic\n(replicated) storage and renames the claim so Argo provisions it fresh:\n\n- **`values-prod.yaml`** → `persistence.storageClass: longhorn`\n(replicated across nodes) instead of the k3s default `local-path`. Base\n`values.yaml` keeps `storageClass: \"\"` so local/kind renders still fall\nback to the cluster default.\n- **Rename the claim** `fuzex-fuzex-data` → `fuzex-design-frames-data`\nvia a dedicated `fuzex.dataClaimName` helper in\n`templates/_helpers.tpl`. It was `fuzex.fullname`-derived (and thus\ncoupled to the Deployment name); a distinct name lets Argo create a\n**fresh** longhorn claim instead of re-binding the stranded local-path\none. Both `templates/pvc.yaml` and `templates/deployment.yaml` reference\nthe helper so name and `claimName` cannot drift.\n\nThe old local-path claim is **left behind** and nothing is lost:\n- the PVC carries `helm.sh/resource-policy: keep`, and\n- the Argo Application runs `prune: false`\n(`deploy/argocd/application.yaml:65`) — confirmed — so Argo will not\ncollect it, and\n- the pod never ran, so the old claim holds no features/frames/approvals\nto migrate.\n\nNo `fuzeinfra.io/durable=true:NoSchedule` toleration added — longhorn is\nnode-agnostic, so the pod needs no affinity to durable nodes (task\ndefault: do not add).\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n- [ ] New feature\n- [ ] Breaking change\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [ ] Chore / CI / refactor\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Branch named `feat/…`, `fix/…`, or `chore/…`\n- [x] Conventional commit messages\n- [x] Commits are **signed** (verified)\n- [ ] Tests added/updated where relevant — n/a, chart-only change\n- [x] **Harden Gate** checks pass — validated locally, see below (CI is\nauthoritative)\n- [ ] Conversations resolved and ready for code-owner review\n\n### Validation\n\nMirrors `.github/workflows/helm-validate.yml` (`helm lint` + `helm\ntemplate | kubeconform -strict -kubernetes-version 1.29.0\n-ignore-missing-schemas`, base values and prod overlay):\n\n```\nhelm lint (base):        1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed\nhelm lint (prod):        1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed\nkubeconform (base):      1 resource found  — Valid: 1, Invalid: 0, Errors: 0\nkubeconform (prod):      7 resources found — Valid: 7, Invalid: 0, Errors: 0\n```\n\nRendered prod PVC and Deployment (excerpt):\n\n```\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\n  name: fuzex-design-frames-data\n  annotations: { helm.sh/resource-policy: keep }\nspec:\n  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]\n  storageClassName: \"longhorn\"\n  resources: { requests: { storage: \"5Gi\" } }\n---\nkind: Deployment\n  name: fuzex-fuzex          # unchanged\n    volumes: [{ name: data, persistentVolumeClaim: { claimName: fuzex-design-frames-data } }]\n```\n\n## Related issues\n\nFuzeInfra#980 (self-registration init container never completed for ns\n`fuzex`).\n\n> **Do not merge yet.** Runtime verification (`-n fuzex get pods` →\n`Running`, `GET /api/v1/app-registry/apps/fuzex` → activated) can only\nbe produced after this merges and Argo syncs, since nothing deploys from\nthe branch. Merge during a normal deploy window.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UJ2RFqo56VLki81TQhwu3f\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJ2RFqo56VLki81TQhwu3f)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: fuzeone-bot <fuzeone-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf9aab00be9b2b4a3c8763c779db7052073f67d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/cf9aab00be9b2b4a3c8763c779db7052073f67d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/6587857bf392d8148a034b443fdab982242fae35","verification":{"payload":"tree cf9aab00be9b2b4a3c8763c779db7052073f67d2\nparent 61e46434bd633e33fcaec0ed9294124e74e3c204\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1790158768 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790158768 +0300\n\nfix(deploy): unblock FuzeX portal self-registration (#81)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `design-frames-service` pod carries the FuzeFront self-registration\ninit container — the thing that puts FuzeX in the FuzeFront portal menu.\nIn prod it has been `Pending` for 7d+ with `0/N nodes available: …\ndidn''t match PersistentVolume''s node affinity` on PVC\n`fuzex-fuzex-data`: a **local-path** PV pinned to a since-tainted node.\nA local-path PV binds to a single node, so once that node was tainted\nthe claim''s pod could never schedule anywhere — and never registered.\nThis is the node-local-storage-for-a-stateful-pod failure class\n(FuzeInfra#980; the same loss took three local-path PVs in\nFuzeInfra#924).\n\nThis PR moves the design-store persistence onto node-agnostic\n(replicated) storage and renames the claim so Argo provisions it fresh:\n\n- **`values-prod.yaml`** → `persistence.storageClass: longhorn`\n(replicated across nodes) instead of the k3s default `local-path`. Base\n`values.yaml` keeps `storageClass: \"\"` so local/kind renders still fall\nback to the cluster default.\n- **Rename the claim** `fuzex-fuzex-data` → `fuzex-design-frames-data`\nvia a dedicated `fuzex.dataClaimName` helper in\n`templates/_helpers.tpl`. It was `fuzex.fullname`-derived (and thus\ncoupled to the Deployment name); a distinct name lets Argo create a\n**fresh** longhorn claim instead of re-binding the stranded local-path\none. Both `templates/pvc.yaml` and `templates/deployment.yaml` reference\nthe helper so name and `claimName` cannot drift.\n\nThe old local-path claim is **left behind** and nothing is lost:\n- the PVC carries `helm.sh/resource-policy: keep`, and\n- the Argo Application runs `prune: false`\n(`deploy/argocd/application.yaml:65`) — confirmed — so Argo will not\ncollect it, and\n- the pod never ran, so the old claim holds no features/frames/approvals\nto migrate.\n\nNo `fuzeinfra.io/durable=true:NoSchedule` toleration added — longhorn is\nnode-agnostic, so the pod needs no affinity to durable nodes (task\ndefault: do not add).\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n- [ ] New feature\n- [ ] Breaking change\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [ ] Chore / CI / refactor\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Branch named `feat/…`, `fix/…`, or `chore/…`\n- [x] Conventional commit messages\n- [x] Commits are **signed** (verified)\n- [ ] Tests added/updated where relevant — n/a, chart-only change\n- [x] **Harden Gate** checks pass — validated locally, see below (CI is\nauthoritative)\n- [ ] Conversations resolved and ready for code-owner review\n\n### Validation\n\nMirrors `.github/workflows/helm-validate.yml` (`helm lint` + `helm\ntemplate | kubeconform -strict -kubernetes-version 1.29.0\n-ignore-missing-schemas`, base values and prod overlay):\n\n```\nhelm lint (base):        1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed\nhelm lint (prod):        1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed\nkubeconform (base):      1 resource found  — Valid: 1, Invalid: 0, Errors: 0\nkubeconform (prod):      7 resources found — Valid: 7, Invalid: 0, Errors: 0\n```\n\nRendered prod PVC and Deployment (excerpt):\n\n```\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\n  name: fuzex-design-frames-data\n  annotations: { helm.sh/resource-policy: keep }\nspec:\n  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]\n  storageClassName: \"longhorn\"\n  resources: { requests: { storage: \"5Gi\" } }\n---\nkind: Deployment\n  name: fuzex-fuzex          # unchanged\n    volumes: [{ name: data, persistentVolumeClaim: { claimName: fuzex-design-frames-data } }]\n```\n\n## Related issues\n\nFuzeInfra#980 (self-registration init container never completed for ns\n`fuzex`).\n\n> **Do not merge yet.** Runtime verification (`-n fuzex get pods` →\n`Running`, `GET /api/v1/app-registry/apps/fuzex` → activated) can only\nbe produced after this merges and Argo syncs, since nothing deploys from\nthe branch. Merge during a normal deploy window.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UJ2RFqo56VLki81TQhwu3f\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJ2RFqo56VLki81TQhwu3f)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: fuzeone-bot <fuzeone-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs6ewCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd34QAAW0MPUH3oUMegVqzKovhO6+\nzPciKEi3P0tZi1ABEiS5WU+KNMkcKf/4EjhMjNhJqfb0N6St2u2RYeZHBNvHRCOY\nWWsjqsebazYgW7++p8cDnStTbpDpie0oh3aqwOCm1BH0CbMkUDYqfMv8N+IKalDn\n74Zx0BgnDQD5/nvJOtk6u9xoBdF+RqY4NlaZEOh9FOr9lZNJ0QtqRRM