commits/1ddd283270eea7f9ccfac9f8a331acca0d6322f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/291ccb22111e59a4885ceda5fbd0312b14c8b760/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:38:36Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:38:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): vendor telegram-pr-merged + fuze-ci-autofix so they can actually run (FuzeInfra#758) (#73)\n\n## Why\n\nA **PUBLIC repo cannot resolve a reusable workflow hosted in a PRIVATE\nrepo.** These workflows called\n`izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-*.yml@main`; FuzeSDLC is\nprivate, so on every affected consumer the job failed at **startup**\n(\"workflow was not found\") and **never ran once** — silently, with no\nred tick.\n\nTracked as FuzeInfra#758.\n\n## What\n\nReplaces the `workflow_call` boundary with the **inlined,\nself-contained** canonical from `FuzeSDLC/workflow-templates/` (already\nfixed there; the hub could not propagate it — see below).\n\nWith the `workflow_call` boundary gone, secrets are read **directly** as\n`secrets.X` rather than declared as required inputs. A missing\n`TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`/`TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` is a **clean skip, not a\nfailure**.\n\n## Why per-repo PRs and not governance-sync\n\n`scripts/governance_sync.py` reconciles `.github/workflows/**` **only\nwhen `--write-workflows` is passed**, and that flag is gated on a\nworkflows-scoped `fuze-agent` App token that **does not yet exist**\n(granting `workflows: write` is a human action in the GitHub UI). Until\nthen the sweep is **detect-only** for workflows. That is precisely why\nthe canonical fix has sat unpropagated. So the per-repo PR is the\nnecessary path — and it will **not** be reverted today.\n\n## Byte-exactness\n\nThe file is not hand-copied: it is generated through the same\n`lib.render` call `governance_sync.py` and the bootstrap installer use,\nwith this repo''s own `default_branch`, `baselineRef` and `ci.runner`. It\ntherefore lands **in sync**, not as fresh drift.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"41937b177a0fbab30bc48508e640284e1f799c7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/41937b177a0fbab30bc48508e640284e1f799c7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/291ccb22111e59a4885ceda5fbd0312b14c8b760","verification":{"payload":"tree 41937b177a0fbab30bc48508e640284e1f799c7d\nparent ab3d5356207294a00e1bf034604a6f123bdba47c\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1788302316 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788302316 +0300\n\nfix(ci): vendor telegram-pr-merged + fuze-ci-autofix so they can actually run (FuzeInfra#758) (#73)\n\n## Why\n\nA **PUBLIC repo cannot resolve a reusable workflow hosted in a PRIVATE\nrepo.** These workflows called\n`izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-*.yml@main`; FuzeSDLC is\nprivate, so on every affected consumer the job failed at **startup**\n(\"workflow was not found\") and **never ran once** — silently, with no\nred tick.\n\nTracked as FuzeInfra#758.\n\n## What\n\nReplaces the `workflow_call` boundary with the **inlined,\nself-contained** canonical from `FuzeSDLC/workflow-templates/` (already\nfixed there; the hub could not propagate it — see below).\n\nWith the `workflow_call` boundary gone, secrets are read **directly** as\n`secrets.X` rather than declared as required inputs. A missing\n`TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`/`TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` is a **clean skip, not a\nfailure**.\n\n## Why per-repo PRs and not governance-sync\n\n`scripts/governance_sync.py` reconciles `.github/workflows/**` **only\nwhen `--write-workflows` is passed**, and that flag is gated on a\nworkflows-scoped `fuze-agent` App token that **does not yet exist**\n(granting `workflows: write` is a human action in the GitHub UI). Until\nthen the sweep is **detect-only** for workflows. That is precisely why\nthe canonical fix has sat unpropagated. So the per-repo PR is the\nnecessary path — and it will **not** be reverted today.\n\n## Byte-exactness\n\nThe file is not hand-copied: it is generated through the same\n`lib.render` call `governance_sync.py` and the bootstrap installer use,\nwith this repo''s own `default_branch`, `baselineRef` and `ci.runner`. It\ntherefore lands **in sync**, not as fresh drift.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql1PsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkAwQADDi3oxtjxEN7gxuOMTEY3PX\ncmD7Hx2E1q629jXS0z8BelBY/xJfe3pSpPsmEFoH8q0UPw6ZC6S1cxkyJ17FpU2d\n6bK8/jmLCnqH2HKY7u+mD6o3rzXn0wNKhVW1HTsx50pxSY+m8gcHwn5