_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/ab3d5356207294a00e1bf034604a6f123bdba47c","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKGFiM2Q1MzU2MjA3Mjk0YTAwZTFiZjAzNDYwNGE2ZjEyM2JkYmE0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/c3253e5f455cd0265396f45650959f0bdd4cbed1","sha":"c3253e5f455cd0265396f45650959f0bdd4cbed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/c3253e5f455cd0265396f45650959f0bdd4cbed1"}],"sha":"ab3d5356207294a00e1bf034604a6f123bdba47c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/ab3d5356207294a00e1bf034604a6f123bdba47c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/c3253e5f455cd0265396f45650959f0bdd4cbed1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:35:09Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:35:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(sdlc): fleet parity with canonical workflow + action templates (#66)\n\n## What this is\n\nThe per-repo half of a fleet-parity sweep against the canonical\n`workflow-templates/` + `.github/actions/` in `izzywdev/FuzeSDLC`.\n\nProduced by the canonical installer, not by hand:\n`scripts/bootstrap/main.py --only workflows`. Every workflow file\ncarries the\n`fuze:managed` marker, `runs-on:` is rendered from this repo''s declared\n`ci.runner` by `lib/render.py` (no hand-pinned runner classes), and\n`.fuze/installed.json` records exactly what landed.\n\n## Root cause (read this first)\n\nThis repo is **not** misconfigured. `governance/versioning.md` says\nrepos pin the\nmoving `v1` alias, and `v1` has pointed at `1585ea1` (v1.9.0,\n2026-08-21) while\nFuzeSDLC `main` advanced to `709de56` — **92 commits**. Everything below\nis\nsimply what never got released.\n\nThe release request is **izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#268** (`baseline-version.txt`\n→\n`1.10.0`). **Merge that first.** This PR installs from `709de56`, the\nexact\ncommit `v1.10.0` will be cut at, so once the alias moves the two agree\nbyte-for-byte and `governance-sync` reports `CURRENT`.\n\n## Why this needed a PR at all\n\n`governance_sync.py` reconciles `.github/actions/**` and skills/agents\non every\nPR — but it **reports** an absent `.github/workflows/*.yml` and\ndeliberately\nnever installs one (first-write belongs to `sdlc-bootstrap`, which seeds\nthe\nmarker with it). So absent workflow files are the one class the\nautomatic loop\ncannot close.\n\n## BEFORE → AFTER\n\n### Workflow templates that were absent (4)\n- `.github/workflows/fuze-ci-autofix.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/gate-required-checks.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/fuze-code-review.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/gate-workflow-drift.yml`\n\n### Composite actions reconciled (9)\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/action.yml` — STALE COPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/classify.sh` — STALE COPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/__tests__/test_classify.sh` — STALE\nCOPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/__tests__/test_extra_env.py` — STALE\nCOPY\n-\n`.github/actions/fuze-code-action/__tests__/test_passthrough_defaults.py`\n— STALE COPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/__tests__/test_rung_gating.py` —\nSTALE COPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/__tests__/test_run_blocks_parse.py`\n— STALE COPY\n- `.github/actions/fuze-push-identity/action.yml` — ABSENT\n- `.github/actions/llm-endpoint/action.yml` — STALE COPY\n\n### Gate scripts / self-tests the new workflows shell out to (10)\n- `scripts/gate_api_version.py`\n- `scripts/gate_vacuous_check.py`\n- `scripts/gate_federation_contract.py`\n- `scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `scripts/gate_workflow_drift.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_gate_api_version.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_gate_vacuous_check.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_gate_federation_contract.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_gate_workflow_drift.py`\n\n### Governance policy data (2)\n- `governance/federation-contract-policy.json`\n- `governance/workflow-drift-policy.json`\n\n## Deliberately NOT touched\n\n- **`a2a-maintain.yml`** — the canonical is being rewritten right now;\nstamping\nthe current version would distribute a copy that is about to change.\nExcluded\n  at the installer level and re-verified against `HEAD` after every run.\n- **18 file(s) that differ from the canonical with a local edit or no\nprovenance record** (`CONFLICT` / `LOCAL` / `UNTRACKED`). The installer\nleaves\nthese alone by default and so does this PR — `--adopt-canonical` was\n**not**\n  used. Resolving them is a separate, reviewable decision:\n- `.github/workflows/claude.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/claude-auto-pr.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/governance-nightly.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/telegram-pr-merged.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/harden-gate.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/gate-line-endings.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/gate-fuze-code-action.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/governance-sync.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/label-sync.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/publish-expert.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/nightly-integration.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/design-approval.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/gate-frames-stamped.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/pages-frames.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/design-review-notify.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/helm-validate.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/mcp-maintain.yml`\n\n## Check state — honest\n\nSelf-hosted CI cannot currently run fleet-wide: the ARC `ci` pool is 2\nfixed\nnodes with ~40 runner pods `Pending`, and the autoscaler only grows an\n`elastic`\npool that runner pods cannot select. Expect checks **queued/blocked**,\nnot\ngreen. Not worked around — switching `runs-on:` to `ubuntu-latest` would\nbe a\npolicy change, not a fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: fuzeone-bot <fuzeone-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8182585aa7a022431443240d393d808402a6ae5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/8182585aa7a022431443240d393d808402a6ae5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/c3253e5f455cd0265396f45650959f0bdd4cbed1","verification":{"payload":"tree 8182585aa7a022431443240d393d808402a6ae5f\nparent 19d00ef86b0078f9ab521a815dda63737b072e8f\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1788269709 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788269709 +0300\n\nchore(sdlc): fleet parity with canonical workflow + action templates (#66)\n\n## What this is\n\nThe per-repo half of a fleet-parity sweep against the canonical\n`workflow-templates/` + `.github/actions/` in `izzywdev/FuzeSDLC`.\n\nProduced by the canonical installer, not by hand:\n`scripts/bootstrap/main.py --only workflows`. Every workflow file\ncarries the\n`fuze:managed` marker, `runs-on:` is rendered from this repo''s declared\n`ci.runner` by `lib/render.py` (no hand-pinned runner classes), and\n`.fuze/installed.js