rs/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/553eb2c94b932f7c7e9982317c5924ab6df9fd87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:10:43Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:10:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(governance): bootstrap + reconcile FuzeX to FuzeSDLC baseline + install canonical skills (#59)\n\n* chore(governance): bootstrap + reconcile FuzeX to FuzeSDLC baseline + install canonical skills\n\nRuns the sanctioned sdlc-bootstrap engine against FuzeX at its pinned\nbaselineRef (v1, newer than FuzeX''s Aug-17 install), applying only safe,\nforward reconciliations and leaving repo-diverged workflows untouched.\n\nBootstrap (from FuzeSDLC v1):\n- Add gate-api-version gate script + its test (were absent).\n- Add .github/actionlint.yaml (community).\n- Add private-registry .npmrc for packages/identity and the two\n  design-frames-service package roots.\n- Forward-update gate_identifier.py (+test), gate_ds_conformance.py,\n  check-registration.mjs, sync-chart-files.sh, and four skill SKILL.md\n  files the repo never edited (canonical moved v1-ward).\n- Refresh the .fuze/installed.json provenance ledger.\n\nGovernance skills (installed out-of-band; not agent-referenced, so the\nbootstrap skills cap does not carry them, but governance-nightly runs\ngovernance-reconciliation and repo-cleaner runs on demand):\n- governance-reconciliation, sdlc-bootstrap (from v1)\n- repo-cleaner, branch-audit (post-v1; sourced from FuzeSDLC main)\n\nUntouched by design: MIT LICENSE (oss-public), Node 24 / React 19\ntoolchain floor, baselineRef (stays v1), and 15 repo-diverged managed\nworkflows left for hand review rather than downgraded.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(governance): keep gate_identifier + check-registration at repo baseline (unbreak Harden Gate)\n\nThe v1 forward-updates of these two gate scripts break FuzeX CI, because\nFuzeX''s surrounding content is main-era, not v1:\n\n- scripts/gate_identifier.py (+ test): v1''s polymorphic composed-schema\n  suite (allOf/oneOf/anyOf) fails 12 cases in the CI runner''s Python env\n  (passes locally), reddening Harden Gate''s gate-identifier job.\n- scripts/check-registration.mjs: v1 adds a \"launcher label must not carry\n  the Fuze prefix\" rule that FuzeX''s existing registration/manifest.json\n  (name/menuLabel \"FuzeX\") violates — a product-facing rename, not a\n  governance mechanic to force here.\n\nReverted both to the repo''s current (green) versions and restored their\nprovenance-ledger entries. All other v1 reconciliations from the previous\ncommit stand. Adopting these two belongs in dedicated follow-ups (and is\nfurther evidence the baselineRef=v1 pin lags FuzeX''s main-era content).\n\n* fix(governance): drop gate-api-version (FuzeX CI runner lacks PyYAML)\n\nThe v1 gate-api-version script + test cannot run in FuzeX''s harden-gate\nrunner: it has no PyYAML, so the gate fails closed (\"PyYAML is not\ninstalled ... Failing closed\") and its self-test asserts on output the\ngate cannot produce (and the v1 test also mismatches the gate''s message\ncase). harden-gate has no gate-api-version job that needs the script, and\nmaster never carried it, so removing both matches the repo''s green state.\n\nThis is the same missing-PyYAML gap that made v1''s gate_identifier\ncomposed-schema walk return 0 in CI. Adopting either belongs in a\nfollow-up that first adds pyyaml to the harden-gate environment.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b65ce0ea6fe97b7cac693b4be8067a5d8ee4ec80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/b65ce0ea6fe97b7cac693b4be8067a5d8ee4ec80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/553eb2c94b932f7c7e9982317c5924ab6df9fd87","verification":{"payload":"tree b65ce0ea6fe97b7cac693b4be8067a5d8ee4ec80\nparent 797cd03084f470e6ce23c4b8c6f4b76e47d4c46f\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787832643 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787832643 +0300\n\nchore(governance): bootstrap + reconcile FuzeX to FuzeSDLC baseline + install canonical skills (#59)\n\n* chore(governance): bootstrap + reconcile FuzeX to FuzeSDLC baseline + install canonical skills\n\nRuns the sanctioned sdlc-bootstrap engine against FuzeX at its pinned\nbaselineRef (v1, newer than FuzeX''s Aug-17 install), applying only safe,\nforward reconciliations and leaving repo-diverged workflows untouched.\n\nBootstrap (from FuzeSDLC v1):\n- Add gate-api-version gate script + its test (were absent).\n- Add .github/actionlint.yaml (community).\n- Add private-registry .npmrc for packages/identity and the two\n  design-frames-service package roots.\n- Forward-update gate_identifier.py (+test), gate_ds_conformance.py,\n  check-registration.mjs, sync-chart-files.sh, and four skill SKILL.md\n  files the repo never edited (canonical moved v1-ward).\n- Refresh the .fuze/installed.json provenance ledger.\n\nGovernance skills (installed out-of-band; not agent-referenced, so the\nbootstrap skills cap does not carry them, but governance-nightly runs\ngovernance-reconciliation and repo-cleaner runs on demand):\n- governance-reconciliation, sdlc-bootstrap (from v1)\n- repo-cleaner, branch-audit (post-v1; sourced from FuzeSDLC main)\n\nUntouched by design: MIT LICENSE (oss-public), Node 24 / React 19\ntoolchain floor, baselineRef (stays v1), and 15 repo-diverged managed\nworkflows left for hand review rather than downgraded.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(governance): keep gate_identifier + check-registration at repo baseline (unbreak Harden Gate)\n\nThe v1 forward-updates of these two gate scripts break FuzeX CI, because\nFuzeX''s surrounding content is main-era, not v1:\n\n- scripts/gate_identifier.py (+ test): v1''s polymorphic composed-schema\n  suite (allOf/oneOf/anyOf) fails 12 cases in the CI runner''s Python env\n  (passes locally), reddening Harden Gate''s gate-identifier job.\n- scripts/check-registration.mjs: v1 adds a \"launcher label must not carry\n  the Fuze prefix\" rule that FuzeX''s existing registration/manifest.json\n  (name/menuLabel \"FuzeX\") violates — a product-facing rename, not a\n  governance mechanic to force here.\n\nReverted both to the repo''s current (green) versions and restored their\nprovenance-ledger entries. All other v1 reconciliations from the previous\ncommit stand. Adopting these two belongs in dedicated follow-ups (and is\nfurther evidence the baselineRef=v1 pin lags FuzeX''s main-era content).\n\n* fix(governance): drop gate-api-version (FuzeX CI runner lacks PyYAML)\n\nThe v1 gate-api-version script + test cannot run in FuzeX''s harden-gate\nrunner: it has no PyYAML, so the gate fails closed (\"PyYAML is not\ninstalled ... Failing closed\") and its self-test asserts on output the\ngate cannot produce (and the v1 test also mismatches the gate''s message\ncase). harden-gate has no gate-api-version job that needs the script, and\nmaster never carried it, so removing both matches the repo''s green state.\n\nThis is the same missing-PyYAML gap that made v1''s gate_identifier\ncomposed-schema walk return 0 in CI. Adopting either belongs in a\nfollow-up that first adds pyyaml to the harden-gate environment.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkClDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfa8QAF0jR/3PH6BLrWnOcihrEGV+\nZkIy4sWXXhLidbWcLmgxPO2Zl5SRVHCg/0mXaUkmg/N4Nq4p13i2G2r3EUtrYYMm\njujtS3f1r0XquUb2pCepqqQqPj10VXjytowKlVZT+dqdUkopw1vZNhXzzya7UwHm\nBFSE2GUvRJlztBCAXNC5TJ0kl+boYKD5F0O72+U6sjJRLj+gHZVjPpKTWXLy83ss\n/vBSPPkjXKfFMkQWeGgMPlGo/X6O/s9QOy3B7/wLXvVL4+IVr0i9DOpls7SgJWzw\nfW58DzHyEmmJ9YxOxovEBBTctvZIoO1JqlvYv3Vj7nbAky81WwiM5RlTCDLwBoZs\nEIuOr1QjS3DIdDs/T39k1ABN5Re7WWXlwg3+15Wjz74kKUtfTb1aThsbT7alKv2Z\nssuFl3TpGij4xM+xMQSXI9AXYNNmVKlK8jyaiy++SJPHXtt7kYWoPmcY/ZcvluK9\nYV/uWN8XWb/lMPU+wRB9rc5yRd2BtvBErppbxxARA5/PWXk7ehlrFxDunGCtD1A8\nf7m1R2q7/nsiP7GAVDJscNTlupqsqksNhxzyb4T98xmJSxGO5tNsJUft5PYs69km\ny99A19zdvNTCqYYWEQaFdkrZ4OYdDOZc+YiO/ciLC4rMCtDROC9BLElN6K2JsobD\nGCKSKMaaelakIFRdoihg\n=XCRi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T12:10:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_eve