0a4e94f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/73d5ae9da47488ed5793cef264fdc843e77938d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:26:42Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:26:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(release): retry the tag-bump PR, and never discard the bump if it fails (#50)\n\n* fix(release): stop hitting the GraphQL rate limit when opening the tag-bump PR\n\nEvery push-triggered release.yml run for FuzeX has failed at the\n\"Open the tag-bump PR\" step (runs #32632618648, #32632605944) after a\nsuccessful image build+push, with:\n\n    GraphQL: API rate limit already exceeded for user ID 99821070\n\n`gh pr list` and `gh pr create` both route repository/PR resolution through\ngh''s GraphQL API, and the release identity used across this fleet''s repos\nshares one GraphQL quota that gets exhausted by the volume of releases\nrunning concurrently. So the image gets built and pushed, but the prod\nvalues-prod.yaml tag-bump PR that would actually ship it is never opened —\nArgo keeps syncing the old (nonexistent) pin and FuzeX never deploys, so it\nnever registers with the FuzeFront portal.\n\nReplace both calls with plain REST via `gh api`, which has a much larger,\nseparate quota:\n- `gh pr list --head` -> `gh api \"repos/.../pulls?head=OWNER:BRANCH&state=open\"`\n- `gh pr create --label` -> `gh api -X POST repos/.../pulls` + a separate\n  `gh api repos/.../issues/<n>/labels` call, since the REST pulls-create\n  endpoint has no label parameter.\n\nSame fail-loud behavior preserved: no `|| true`, no swallowed exit codes.\n\nPart of the portal-registration-gap investigation: FuzeX was missing from\nthe FuzeFront portal because it had never deployed (cause A) — this fixes\nthe release pipeline''s own failure mode, distinct from the chart/registration\nfail-closed work already in flight on #32 (rebase/merge conflicts there are\nthat PR''s own scope, not duplicated here).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(release): retry the tag-bump PR, and never discard the bump if it fails\n\nMeasured 2026-08-25: the image built, deploy/helm/fuzex/values-prod.yaml was\nbumped in-workspace from 6aa1c11f6aff to 4a0212dcf891, and then the step that\nopens the bump PR died with \"API rate limit already exceeded for user ID ...\".\nThe computed bump was thrown away. The prod tag has not moved since\n2026-08-21.\n\nThis is NOT a missing credential — GH_RELEASE_PAT is set here, and the run log\nsays so (\"release credential: GH_RELEASE_PAT\"). The cause is account-wide: one\nuser identity drives every repo''s release automation in this fleet, so a\nsingle API quota gates all of them and is regularly exhausted. That cannot be\nfixed from inside this workflow. What this change fixes is the repo quietly\ndestroying a finished build whenever it happens.\n\n1. THE BUMP IS PRESERVED BEFORE ANY API CALL IS MADE.\n\n   The branch is now committed and pushed first, and the \"is a PR already\n   open?\" lookup happens after. `git push` and `git ls-remote` speak the git\n   protocol, not the REST/GraphQL API, so they are unaffected by the quota\n   that fails this step; once the push lands, the bump is durable on origin\n   and the release can be finished by hand or by a re-run.\n\n   Deliberately NOT an artifact upload: artifact storage is itself exhausted\n   account-wide in this fleet right now (\"Artifact storage quota has been\n   hit\"), so an upload would add a new failure mode instead of a safety net —\n   and a branch is better preservation anyway, being already in the shape the\n   PR needs. A re-run is safe: if the branch already exists on origin its\n   commit IS the bump, so it is left alone rather than force-pushed.\n\n2. EVERY API CALL RETRIES, ON GITHUB''S OWN SIGNALS.\n\n   `gh api -i` keeps the response headers, so the wait comes from what GitHub\n   reported rather than a blind fixed sleep: Retry-After when present\n   (secondary limit), else x-ratelimit-reset when x-ratelimit-remaining is 0\n   (primary limit), else exponential backoff — all with jitter, so concurrent\n   releases across the fleet do not wake together and re-exhaust the shared\n   quota. Bounded by 6 attempts AND a 900s total wall-clock budget, so the job\n   cannot hold a runner for an hour waiting on an hourly reset. Only 403/429,\n   5xx and no-response are retried; 401/404/422 mean the request is wrong and\n   will still be wrong later, so they fail immediately.\n\n3. EXHAUSTION FAILS LOUDLY AND LEGIBLY.\n\n   No `|| true`, no continue-on-error — an unbumped prod must be red. The\n   failure writes a ::error:: and a job-summary block naming that the image\n   WAS built and pushed, that the tag was NOT bumped, which branch the bump is\n   sitting on, and how to finish the release. \"Nothing happened\" never appears\n   without a printed reason next to it.\n\nVerified locally by driving the extracted step script against a stub `gh`:\nrecovery after transient 403s, budget exhaustion into fail_loud, and immediate\nnon-retry of a 422. Verified by actionlint and `bash -n`.\n\nUnverified: this only runs in CI, so no real release has exercised it. Nothing\nabout the account-wide quota is fixed here — the durable fix is to stop\nfunnelling every repo''s release automation through one user PAT and give it\nits own identity.\n\nNot changed: what the bump targets, and the Helm values themselves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8633e4426b907896730e37173af4e11659ce576e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/8633e4426b907896730e37173af4e11659ce576e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/73d5ae9da47488ed5793cef264fdc843e77938d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 8633e4426b907896730e37173af4e11659ce576e\nparent 88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787808402 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787808402 +0300\n\nfix(release): retry the tag-bump PR, and never discard the bump if it fails (#50)\n\n* fix(release): stop hitting the GraphQL rate limit when opening the tag-bump PR\n\nEvery push-triggered release.yml run for FuzeX has failed at the\n\"Open the tag-bump PR\" step (runs #32632618648, #32632605944) after a\nsuccessful image build+push, with:\n\n    GraphQL: API rate limit already exceeded for user ID 99821070\n\n`gh pr list` and `gh pr create` both route repository/PR resolution through\ngh''s GraphQL API, and the release identity used across this fleet''s repos\nshares one GraphQL quota that gets exhausted by the volume of releases\nrunning concurrently. So the image gets built and pushed, but the prod\nvalues-prod.yaml tag-bump PR that would actually ship it is never opened —\nArgo keeps syncing the old (nonexistent) pin and FuzeX never deploys, so it\nnever registers with the FuzeFront portal.\n\nReplace both calls with plain REST via `gh api`, which has a much larger,\nseparate quota:\n- `gh pr list --head` -> `gh api \"repos/.../pulls?head=OWNER:BRANCH&state=open\"`\n- `gh pr create --label` -> `gh api -X POST repos/.../pulls` + a separate\n  `gh api repos/.../issues/<n>/labels` call, since the REST pulls-create\n  endpoint has no label parameter.\n\nSame fail-loud behavior preserved: no `|| true`, no swallowed exit codes.\n\nPart of the portal-registration-gap investigation: FuzeX was missing from\nthe FuzeFront portal because it had never deployed (cause A) — this fixes\nthe release pipeline''s own failure mode, distinct from the chart/registration\nfail-closed work already in flight on #32 (rebase/merge conflicts there are\nthat PR''s own scope, not duplicated here).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(release): retry the tag-bump PR, and never discard the bump if it fails\n\nMeasured 2026-08-25: the image built, deploy/helm/fuzex/values-prod.yaml was\nbumped in-workspace from 6aa1c11f6aff to 4a0212dcf891, and then the step that\nopens the bump PR died with \"API rate limit already exceeded for user ID ...\".\nThe computed bump was thrown away. The prod tag has not moved since\n2026-08-21.\n\nThis is NOT a missing credential — GH_RELEASE_PAT is set here, and the run log\nsays so (\"release credential: GH_RELEASE_PAT\"). The cause is account-wide: one\nuser identity drives every repo''s release automation in this fleet, so a\nsingle API quota gates all of them and is regularly exhausted. That cannot be\nfixed from inside this workflow. What this change fixes is the repo quietly\ndestroying a finished build whenever it happens.\n\n1. THE BUMP IS PRESERVED BEFORE ANY API CALL IS MADE.\n\n   The branch is now committed and pushed first, and the \"is a PR already\n   open?\" lookup happens after. `git push` and `git ls-remote` speak the git\n   protocol, not the REST/GraphQL API, so they are unaffected by the quota\n   that fails this step; once the push lands, the bump is durable on origin\n   and the release can be finished by hand or by a re-run.\n\n   Deliberately NOT an artifact upload: artifact storage is itself exhausted\n   account-wide in this fleet right now (\"Artifact storage quota has been\n   hit\"), so an upload would add a new failure mode instead of a safety net —\n   and a branch is better preservation anyway, being already in the shape the\n   PR needs. A re-run is safe: if the branch already exists on origin its\n   commit IS the bump, so it is left alone rather than force-pushed.\n\n2. EVERY API CALL RETRIES, ON GITHUB''S OWN SIGNALS.\n\n   `gh api -i` keeps the response headers, so the wait comes from what GitHub\n   reported rather than a blind fixed sleep: Retry-After when present\n   (secondary limit), else x-ratelimit-reset when x-ratelimit-remaining is 0\n   (primary limit), else exponential backoff — all with jitter, so concurrent\n   releases across the fleet do not wake together and re-exhaust the shared\n   quota. Bounded by 6 attempts AND a 900s total wall-clock budget, so the job\n   cannot hold a runner for an hour waiting on an hourly reset. Only 403/429,\n   5xx and no-response are retried; 401/404/422 mean the request is wrong and\n   will still be wrong later, so they fail immediately.\n\n3. EXHAUSTION FAILS LOUDLY AND LEGIBLY.\n\n   No `|| true`, no continue-on-error — an unbumped prod must be red. The\n   failure writes a ::error:: and a job-summary block naming that the image\n   WAS built and pushed, that the tag was NOT bumped, which branch the bump is\n   sitting on, and how to finish the release. \"Nothing happened\" never appears\n   without a printed reason next to it.\n\nVerified locally by driving the extracted step script against a stub `gh`:\nrecovery after transient 403s, budget exhaustion into fail_loud, and immediate\nnon-retry of a 422. Verified by actionlint and `bash -n`.\n\nUnverified: this only runs in CI, so no real release has exercised it. Nothing\nabout the account-wide quota is fixed here — the durable fix is to stop\nfunnelling every repo''s release automation through one user PAT and give it\nits own identity.\n\nNot changed: what the bump targets, and the Helm values themselves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj8qSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbH0QAAgaVodUB9XlyS/fmGvVplSd\nMcYUbP1riSN83WgTZWF3agb6KmtpKicHdYiw2EA+3Il9wfmvCsIAIzVR2eoPlCKB\nZk0dH0wa2yfCELi2fuIfPVKuZ/obvwg0r8wZIMrrvI8a7beyNwROW0B2K9Fu48ZX\nVwlGs3jwR6aUAQBvjhFpbmuySnvd2i4vSHTPEj+L0J36ESWXCpbcR/G49L1Nwe1Y\n6r/PvkEMrfLVjbgv+WlMLRMAVA32qmFhyQQQb2uqZeHqXuFZ+/uk5n4J0qk909Tb\nMaO22vamTcPMDSW+R2nHeQrfYwGPtd3kgMrYwA5qxtugHl6+2rTn37vVGzAaQkZa\nxM3la/kHbXLUKtNPmbjd9lq13H5xMh8IkGtL8r7tY9HRowPYVQ6C6kbfGemHxFPa\nDcrOBZaLv+uoy0TWO7XdrKBgZacfPDVHWu2iKt0N/A0I4cRkdGbAS0ltB3VpD1qj\nt/Acq6ED84bK2M8SZgih8dFHyJC8XxmyUzk5kbXxvZlpZyVdM2xGYwDAa6x0lfAh\ngXEbGs2NWdeWoich7IC0Lb7MUDLw2clyQbdbBrnumV/D8QBKEHm83Zn/SkMcIcDH\nT0xrqiBAtai4GnaRK8+VgJgA1Um8WOwVXb4+kjsbf+uHHlD+2dIw2WXV0/QaxatR\n5IZesOlhP7b3xnphC8CI\n=i2D8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T05:26:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/73d5ae9da47488ed5793cef264fdc843e77938d3","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDczZDVhZTlkYTQ3NDg4ZWQ1NzkzY2VmMjY0ZmRjODQzZTc3OTM4ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88","sha":"88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88"}],"sha":"73d5ae9da47488ed5793cef264fdc843e77938d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/73d5ae9da47488ed5793cef264fdc843e77938d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:26:31Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:26:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames-service): migrate MF remote to nginx serving stage (#51)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): migrate MF remote to nginx serving stage\n\nFuzeX served its Module-Federation remote (webapp/''s built dist/) from\nserver.js''s own hand-rolled static-file route — the family''s one\nNode/Express-style serving deviation from the nginx-serving-stage standard\nevery other remote uses, and the reason the federation gate''s layer-4\n(nginx conf) extractor could not read this repo.\n\n- Dockerfile: new `webapp-mfe` target (nginx:alpine) reusing the existing\n  webapp-builder stage; vanilla stage no longer copies webapp''s dist or\n  serves it.\n- webapp/nginx.conf: canonical `location ^~ /apps/fuzex/ { alias\n  /usr/share/nginx/html/; }` form, remoteEntry.js no-cache, /health.\n- server.js: removed the /apps/fuzex/ static-file route entirely (one\n  serving path, not two that could drift).\n- Helm: new webapp-mfe Deployment+Service; federated-mount-ingress.yaml now\n  routes /apps/fuzex/* to it instead of design-frames-service''s own Service.\n- release.yml / design-frames-service-ci.yml: build+push+smoke-check the\n  new image; the vanilla image''s smoke check now asserts /apps/fuzex/\n  404s there (regression guard against re-adding a second serving path).\n\nNo slug, path, or registration/manifest.json change — remoteEntry stays\n/apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js throughout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(webapp-mfe): stop dropping inherited headers, and stop serving as root\n\nTwo real Semgrep findings on this PR, both fixed rather than annotated.\n\nHEADER REDEFINITION (5 findings, and the bug was live). nginx `add_header`\ndoes not append to the inherited set — a location block that calls it AT ALL\ndiscards every header inherited from the server block. Each location here\nre-added Access-Control-Allow-Origin but not Access-Control-Allow-Methods, so\nthe Methods header was silently absent from exactly the /apps/fuzex/ locations\nthat serve the federated bundle. Re-listing headers per location would fix\ntoday and break again the first time someone adds a third header to the\nserver block and not to the copies, so the full set now lives in one included\nfile.\n\nThat file is deliberately NOT under conf.d/. The base image auto-includes\nconf.d/*.conf inside the http block, so a snippet there would apply globally\nAND again at every explicit include — emitting each header twice. It sits at\n/etc/nginx/common-headers.conf and is pulled in only where asked for.\n\nMISSING USER (1 error). nginx:alpine runs its master as root. `USER nginx` on\nthat image is not a fix, it is a broken container: an unprivileged process\ncannot bind :80 and cannot write /var/run/nginx.pid or /var/cache/nginx. So\nthe image becomes nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:alpine, which runs as uid 101\nand listens on 8080 — and the port moves with it in all three places that\nmust agree:\n  Dockerfile  EXPOSE 8080 + HEALTHCHECK http://127.0.0.1:8080/health\n  nginx.conf  listen 8080\n  chart       webapp-mfe.yaml containerPort 8080  (Service targetPort is named\n              `http`, so it follows automatically)\n\nVerified: `helm lint --strict` clean; `helm template` against values-prod\nrenders containerPort 8080 for webapp-mfe and leaves the backend on 4400.\nDocker is unavailable in this sandbox, so the image build and the /health\nsmoke test run for the first time in CI on this PR.\n\n* fix(webapp-mfe): align the FOURTH port site, and state the non-root user explicitly\n\nThe previous commit moved this image to nginx-unprivileged on 8080 and said\nthree places had to agree: Dockerfile EXPOSE/HEALTHCHECK, nginx.conf listen,\nand the chart containerPort. There are four. The CI smoke test still ran\n\"docker run -p 4401:80\", publishing a port nothing was listening on, so\ndocker-build went red -- the one check that actually exercises the image.\n\nThat is the same defect class this PR exists to fix: a value written down in\nseveral places, agreeing in most of them. Fixed, and the comment now names all\nfour so the next person does not have to rediscover the count.\n\nAlso adds an explicit USER 101. The unprivileged base already runs as that\nuid, so this changes no behaviour today -- but Semgrep''s\ndockerfile.security.missing-user reads THIS file rather than the base image\nmetadata, and a future edit swapping the base back to nginx:alpine would\nsilently restore root with nothing to catch it. The line puts the requirement\nin the file that has to hold it.\n\nactionlint: same single pre-existing SC2034 before and after, none added.\nhelm lint --strict clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9fe6c471728545ebd3574661fac25572a86564e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/c9fe6c471728545ebd3574661fac25572a86564e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/88ab45334c8260d1d1fe2b6c460adaae0b965e88","verification":{"payload":"tree c9fe6c471728545ebd3574661fac25572a86564e\nparent a7486dc7114445d7061108c9d7a800638a55a759\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787808391 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787808391 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames-service): migrate MF remote to nginx serving stage (#51)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): migrate MF remote to nginx serving stage\n\nFuzeX served its Module-Federation remote (webapp/''s built dist/) from\nserver.js''s own hand-rolled static-file route — the family''s one\nNode/Express-style serving deviation from the nginx-serving-stage standard\nevery other remote uses, and the reason the federation gate''s layer-4\n(nginx conf) extractor could not read this repo.\n\n- Dockerfile: new `webapp-mfe` target (nginx:alpine) reusing the existing\n  webapp-builder stage; vanilla stage no longer copies webapp''s dist or\n  serves it.\n- webapp/nginx.conf: canonical `location ^~ /apps/fuzex/ { alias\n  /usr/share/nginx/html/; }` form, remoteEntry.js no-cache, /health.\n- server.js: removed the /apps/fuzex/ static-file route entirely (one\n  serving path, not two that could drift).\n- Helm: new webapp-mfe Deployment+Service; federated-mount-ingress.yaml now\n  routes /apps/fuzex/* to it instead of design-frames-service''s own Service.\n- release.yml / design-frames-service-ci.yml: build+push+smoke-check the\n  new image; the vanilla image''s smoke check now asserts /apps/fuzex/\n  404s there (regression guard against re-adding a second serving path).\n\nNo slug, path, or registration/manifest.json change — remoteEntry stays\n/apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js throughout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(webapp-mfe): stop dropping inherited headers, and stop serving as root\n\nTwo real Semgrep findings on this PR, both fixed rather than annotated.\n\nHEADER REDEFINITION (5 findings, and the bug was live). nginx `add_header`\ndoes not append to the inherited set — a location block that calls it AT ALL\ndiscards every header inherited from the server block. Each location here\nre-added Access-Control-Allow-Origin but not Access-Control-Allow-Methods, so\nthe Methods header was silently absent from exactly the /apps/fuzex/ locations\nthat serve the federated bundle. Re-listing headers per location would fix\ntoday and break again the first time someone adds a third header to the\nserver block and not to the copies, so the full set now lives in one included\nfile.\n\nThat file is deliberately NOT under conf.d/. The base image auto-includes\nconf.d/*.conf inside the http block, so a snippet there would apply globally\nAND again at every explicit include — emitting each header twice. It sits at\n/etc/nginx/common-headers.conf and is pulled in only where asked for.\n\nMISSING USER (1 error). nginx:alpine runs its master as root. `USER nginx` on\nthat image is not a fix, it is a broken container: an unprivileged process\ncannot bind :80 and cannot write /var/run/nginx.pid or /var/cache/nginx. So\nthe image becomes nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:alpine, which runs as uid 101\nand listens on 8080 — and the port moves with it in all three places that\nmust agree:\n  Dockerfile  EXPOSE 8080 + HEALTHCHECK http://127.0.0.1:8080/health\n  nginx.conf  listen 8080\n  chart       webapp-mfe.yaml containerPort 8080  (Service targetPort is named\n              `http`, so it follows automatically)\n\nVerified: `helm lint --strict` clean; `helm template` against values-prod\nrenders containerPort 8080 for webapp-mfe and leaves the backend on 4400.\nDocker is unavailable in this sandbox, so the image build and the /health\nsmoke test run for the first time in CI on this PR.\n\n* fix(webapp-mfe): align the FOURTH port site, and state the non-root user explicitly\n\nThe previous commit moved this image to nginx-unprivileged on 8080 and said\nthree places had to agree: Dockerfile EXPOSE/HEALTHCHECK, nginx.conf listen,\nand the chart containerPort. There are four. The CI smoke test still ran\n\"docker run -p 4401:80\", publishing a port nothing was listening on, so\ndocker-build went red -- the one check that actually exercises the image.\n\nThat is the same defect class this PR exists to fix: a value written down in\nseveral places, agreeing in most of them. Fixed, and the comment now names all\nfour so the next person does not have to rediscover the count.\n\nAlso adds an explicit USER 101. The unprivileged base already runs as that\nuid, so this changes no behaviour today -- but Semgrep''s\ndockerfile.security.missing-user reads THIS file rather than the base image\nmetadata, and a future edit swapping the base back to nginx:alpine would\nsilently restore root with nothing to catch it. The line puts the requirement\nin the file that has to hold it.\n\nactionlint: same single pre-existing SC2034 before and after, none added.\nhelm lint --strict clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj8qHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn7UQAIrYbyL64XAYzRxE3PS4Y8sw\nyyqgNZswvEHhKP/tVKoxzJZH+b0NzumsJxW/prARrPVE+7FTI4a/ajJPE5GYa9pc\nRUNbDkoxy2mn+5DoNWPc0Ip0nBNrROK6y7dnaJR+n0KJ/V8O4331laLgsW9E4QSy\nFzpPP+QC+OjmKH45xlsxPdHdg0Q96aZvjOs+wX64z0gexnQUg1RnXJ5Z1Z0+UDaK\nMf++MwzFqaQjWyqRS4ZqZvsDmVPDy1r5e/ykN3jw98ndrgHprphTx54oHt4tNv8s\nck/Fwjnsdxs0zjshJKR/zjC/YQFtC3pbnX+gqXwxgBzafCuooASWirXHe39RHK7W\nSMvvCJvx7SKynrwxlg+I/3BCVUFlsi3hoMWu6lGZNOOFIBGq7pHwCh1eSuh6/96C\nPfosStomBEBlAOJ3EjZJ9N+tcmpH9huF65K1gZW2EDFqq6TeyZywoWrKf+Cs6OCY\nsxp1gmoJ5GOkKr01xLkRY+HUaAi6/pw1nC5ReHbPBmVxmztJ+JDUWJm3kTkp1ssK\n8xG1LyQiMnnygx0sRMhzIGO5RLobYAFwAkF8uXBJ9bJe+Uvn9U+ZCsOzO9NAxqzw\nFdsdNQhqEV3PHvaipXiGGwADxBhvFAMR9Hbsnu4i9wCtUUOAzlykPG0yMRwmp2+a\neB/HU4B2LXMRVyQM+c3h\n=5r+R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T05:26:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"http