b1e5fc0c1c8820e0e991fd498df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/3d4193d9ea656b1e5fc0c1c8820e0e991fd498df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/4a0212dcf89112be1a150cec39da9f1cb5ccb0fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:26Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(design-frames-service): independent acceptance suite for the Postgres lifecycle tier (#40)\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service/acceptance/ — a standalone contract/\nacceptance test suite (node --test, ajv-validated against openapi.yaml\nv0.2.0) run against the real backend/dist/app.js and a real local Postgres,\ndeliberately separate from backend/tests/** so the implementation is not\ngrading itself.\n\n85 tests: 77 pass; 8 intentionally-failing tests document real backend\ndefects found against the frozen contract (kept red, not weakened):\n  - a pagination-cursor duplicate/skip bug (millisecond-precision Date\n    truncation vs microsecond timestamptz columns) affecting every\n    cursor-paginated collection\n  - POST /api/v1/features fails validation when the (contractually\n    optional) `description` field is omitted\n  - approve/reject request bodies silently accept properties outside\n    their additionalProperties:false schema\n  - comment create accepts a client-supplied `authorRef` not declared in\n    CommentCreate''s schema\n  - no live route ever creates a frame_ref row, so frame/element\n    discussion targets are unreachable via the running API\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd6eb60dc63c64b186126c9e6ff085bc81a35d64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/dd6eb60dc63c64b186126c9e6ff085bc81a35d64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/4a0212dcf89112be1a150cec39da9f1cb5ccb0fc","verification":{"payload":"tree dd6eb60dc63c64b186126c9e6ff085bc81a35d64\nparent ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787479286 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787479286 +0300\n\ntest(design-frames-service): independent acceptance suite for the Postgres lifecycle tier (#40)\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service/acceptance/ — a standalone contract/\nacceptance test suite (node --test, ajv-validated against openapi.yaml\nv0.2.0) run against the real backend/dist/app.js and a real local Postgres,\ndeliberately separate from backend/tests/** so the implementation is not\ngrading itself.\n\n85 tests: 77 pass; 8 intentionally-failing tests document real backend\ndefects found against the frozen contract (kept red, not weakened):\n  - a pagination-cursor duplicate/skip bug (millisecond-precision Date\n    truncation vs microsecond timestamptz columns) affecting every\n    cursor-paginated collection\n  - POST /api/v1/features fails validation when the (contractually\n    optional) `description` field is omitted\n  - approve/reject request bodies silently accept properties outside\n    their additionalProperties:false schema\n  - comment create accepts a client-supplied `authorRef` not declared in\n    CommentCreate''s schema\n  - no live route ever creates a frame_ref row, so frame/element\n    discussion targets are unreachable via the running API\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqisT2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAopwQAI0r05p9IZhkviS2YVY2ZTTb\nvqg7W2/tqscfMJswTCKIRR+d3Fcpmwb6SaIqMWsEXHjJDQ6mjDOvlqJW91e5mVI1\ndSSCBOpsex9sxQ3t0gdcpyDFLuVH2AJxcf7yzON5UFwKQzqSuciGLTTYpuJbJZA/\nJmD1yjI99eL5ZAs6gdl1KN/VGqLtPKX5lvcsbpEuZx34/3jhew1RBjJgFb/lJHgW\nEZhPWS5ZsnNywOxRA5kEoIbS8Z5WsP0eufrbkRe+IQlVDOmkcx3fojGl/7/tHpJM\nYHn/pDS7lu4tMOq7OXuoLcke8Bs8gpFSAWEV4ZirL+G7ouIhEqjIHVoDCMgQdvla\niUCjKCjEa5+Y8KiQ8iz6cQ9j+O8hZa1otuIUFrU+ApyiGX2X58tDtvBZnVNPjT8v\nUXcOPWjzkj664xSbBWnwyeQDRuCAo3iHt0x7M+Efnyiy12AlL7/w6O7xoLnaxCIw\nlfHYF3CjD9XfKH+wmtVG99KqUbm4nkes8daVgJPOzgscBJKzDWI1QhRmJ9FOcCDF\n/bSbGiZXNoAiqGu2mA+PWMt2r1esr6bEDJdDsyNA/tGs7J1ZKBNRq33qWucpnrsb\nBjnTnXkBQyTMIsold+CtnXwHEIEELFdU0fBh3RcYOxXzH6Rm256cURTIhK+nVmJT\nUu+uEL/w1suvSra6yJVc\n=adCa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T10:01:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/4a0212dcf89112be1a150cec39da9f1cb5ccb0fc","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDRhMDIxMmRjZjg5MTEyYmUxYTE1MGNlYzM5ZGE5ZjFjYjVjY2IwZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958","sha":"ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958"}],"sha":"4a0212dcf89112be1a150cec39da9f1cb5ccb0fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/4a0212dcf89112be1a150cec39da9f1cb5ccb0fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:18Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames-service): deploy/CI wiring for the Postgres lifecycle tier (#43)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): deploy/CI wiring for the Postgres lifecycle tier\n\nPackage backend/ (Express+pg+TS, port 4410) and db/migrate.sh into the Helm\nchart and image build, gated OFF by default until FuzeInfra provisions the\ndatabase, role, schema, and DATABASE_URL SealedSecret.\n\n- Dockerfile: adds an identity-builder + backend-builder + postgres-tier\n  build target (node:24-alpine), unreferenced by and non-disruptive to the\n  existing default (vanilla, node:20-alpine) build target. ONE new image,\n  shared by both the backend Deployment and the migration Job.\n- Helm: postgres-tier Deployment + Service (ClusterIP :4410, /health probes)\n  and a db-migrate Job wired as an Argo CD PreSync hook (this chart is\n  applied only by Argo, never `helm upgrade --install` — see\n  deploy/argocd/application.yaml), matching db/README.md''s own description\n  of the runner as \"a pre-sync Argo/Helm Job\". All new resources gated by\n  postgresTier.enabled: false (values.yaml + values-prod.yaml).\n- CI: release.yml builds/pushes the new postgres-tier image alongside the\n  existing one (same tag, same release) and bumps both tags in\n  values-prod.yaml; design-frames-service-ci.yml adds a build+health smoke\n  check for the new target.\n- deploy/infra-requests/design-frames-postgres.md: the FuzeInfra @claude\n  hand-off — database + design_frames schema + least-privilege role +\n  DATABASE_URL SealedSecret in the fuzex namespace. This repo provisions\n  none of it.\n\nVerified: helm lint clean; helm template renders the postgres-tier\nDeployment/Service/Job under --set postgresTier.enabled=true and passes\nkubeconform -strict; the default (OFF) render is byte-identical to\norigin/master for both values.yaml and values-prod.yaml; actionlint clean\non both touched workflows.\n\n* fix(design-frames-service): fix postgres-tier boot crash, harden CI smoke check\n\nCI (#43) built the postgres-tier image successfully but the container\ncrashed on boot before binding its port, so the /health smoke check timed\nout with zero diagnostic output (the failing bare `curl -sf` exited under\n`set -e` before the `docker logs` line ever ran).\n\nReproduced locally without a Docker daemon (unavailable in this sandbox) by\nrecreating the final stage''s exact node_modules/dist layout with plain\nnpm/node and running `node backend/dist/index.js` directly. Found two\ndistinct MODULE_NOT_FOUND crashes, fixed both, and confirmed a clean boot +\n/health 200 in the same repro:\n\n1. `npm prune --omit=dev` (backend-builder) re-resolves the local `file:`\n   dependency @fuzex/identity back into a relative symlink, discarding the\n   `--install-links` copy from the earlier `npm install`. That symlink only\n   resolves inside the builder stage; it dangles the moment node_modules is\n   copied into the postgres-tier final stage, so `require(''@fuzex/identity'')`\n   (backend/src/lib/identity.ts) throws at boot. Fixed by replacing the\n   prune with a fresh `--omit=dev --install-links` install, which keeps the\n   real copy.\n2. backend/src/lib/{fileStore,manifestSchema,stampLib}.ts each `require()` a\n   sibling of the vanilla service''s own ../lib/{store,schema,stamp}.js at a\n   runtime-computed path (docs/postgres-tier.md''s dual-write projection) —\n   never copied into the postgres-tier image. Fixed by adding `COPY lib/\n   ./lib/` to that stage; confirmed none of the three touch the filesystem\n   at require()-time, so this alone is enough to boot (real dual-write reads\n   /writes still need DESIGN_FRAMES_DATA_DIR pointed at the frontend''s data\n   volume — noted in the Dockerfile, not yet wired into the Deployment).\n\nAlso hardens design-frames-service-ci.yml''s postgres-tier smoke check to\nalways print `docker logs` before asserting pass/fail, so a future\ncrash-on-boot is diagnosable from the CI log directly instead of silently\nskipping straight to a bare timeout.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e716262a262171e976c1f8fda926166489c5bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/1e716262a262171e976c1f8fda926166489c5bec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e716262a262171e976c1f8fda926166489c5bec\nparent 5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787479278 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787479278 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames-service): deploy/CI wiring for the Postgres lifecycle tier (#43)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): deploy/CI wiring for the Postgres lifecycle tier\n\nPackage backend/ (Express+pg+TS, port 4410) and db/migrate.sh into the Helm\nchart and image build, gated OFF by default until FuzeInfra provisions the\ndatabase, role, schema, and DATABASE_URL SealedSecret.\n\n- Dockerfile: adds an identity-builder + backend-builder + postgres-tier\n  build target (node:24-alpine), unreferenced by and non-disruptive to the\n  existing default (vanilla, node:20-alpine) build target. ONE new image,\n  shared by both the backend Deployment and the migration Job.\n- Helm: postgres-tier Deployment + Service (ClusterIP :4410, /health probes)\n  and a db-migrate Job wired as an Argo CD PreSync hook (this chart is\n  applied only by Argo, never `helm upgrade --install` — see\n  deploy/argocd/application.yaml), matching db/README.md''s own description\n  of the runner as \"a pre-sync Argo/Helm Job\". All new resources gated by\n  postgresTier.enabled: false (values.yaml + values-prod.yaml).\n- CI: release.yml builds/pushes the new postgres-tier image alongside the\n  existing one (same tag, same release) and bumps both tags in\n  values-prod.yaml; design-frames-service-ci.yml adds a build+health smoke\n  check for the new target.\n- deploy/infra-requests/design-frames-postgres.md: the FuzeInfra @claude\n  hand-off — database + design_frames schema + least-privilege role +\n  DATABASE_URL SealedSecret in the fuzex namespace. This repo provisions\n  none of it.\n\nVerified: helm lint clean; helm template renders the postgres-tier\nDeployment/Service/Job under --set postgresTier.enabled=true and passes\nkubeconform -strict; the default (OFF) render is byte-identical to\norigin/master for both values.yaml and values-prod.yaml; actionlint clean\non both touched workflows.\n\n* fix(design-frames-service): fix postgres-tier boot crash, harden CI smoke check\n\nCI (#43) built the postgres-tier image successfully but the container\ncrashed on boot before binding its port, so the /health smoke check timed\nout with zero diagnostic output (the failing bare `curl -sf` exited under\n`set -e` before the `docker logs` line ever ran).\n\nReproduced locally without a Docker daemon (unavailable in this sandbox) by\nrecreating the final stage''s exact node_modules/dist layout with plain\nnpm/node and running `node backend/dist/index.js` directly. Found two\ndistinct MODULE_NOT_FOUND crashes, fixed both, and confirmed a clean boot +\n/health 200 in the same repro:\n\n1. `npm prune --omit=dev` (backend-builder) re-resolves the local `file:`\n   dependency @fuzex/identity back into a relative symlink, discarding the\n   `--install-links` copy from the earlier `npm install`. That symlink only\n   resolves inside the builder stage; it dangles the moment node_modules is\n   copied into the postgres-tier final stage, so `require(''@fuzex/identity'')`\n   (backend/src/lib/identity.ts) throws at boot. Fixed by replacing the\n   prune with a fresh `--omit=dev --install-links` install, which keeps the\n   real copy.\n2. backend/src/lib/{fileStore,manifestSchema,stampLib}.ts each `require()` a\n   sibling of the vanilla service''s own ../lib/{store,schema,stamp}.js at a\n   runtime-computed path (docs/postgres-tier.md''s dual-write projection) —\n   never copied into the postgres-tier image. Fixed by adding `COPY lib/\n   ./lib/` to that stage; confirmed none of the three touch the filesystem\n   at require()-time, so this alone is enough to boot (real dual-write reads\n   /writes still need DESIGN_FRAMES_DATA_DIR pointed at the frontend''s data\n   volume — noted in the Dockerfile, not yet wired into the Deployment).\n\nAlso hardens design-frames-service-ci.yml''s postgres-tier smoke check to\nalways print `docker logs` before asserting pass/fail, so a future\ncrash-on-boot is diagnosable from the CI log directly instead of silently\nskipping straight to a bare timeout.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqisTuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD2cQAK5k9EDa9YyzQfHL8vVCUbJL\n99zbZ93BXph4rv3HgTB3brjupnW8mastbQoFCcRKgoN6mfRN1uDEuO3rGEbaOpZV\nHTSX7b0s3R2Bp96+kIP2IkGUU/QxEM9ESWkhySaYw4AQUdtpBlN3fNVW3Pml5COe\nqbzGUuQkhDonQLeH11d1JmUg866/qiKADOTiBb4mVmZ/yrv15eRAnJkpU6IoG1Dz\nBu/qGQZldllEpQAtq668AOjOAndLe27dLZs2lppP0fuQPpkShw9tPQK/JO0Z3keQ\n9bYHV3aezuOnJ8nlKx1gDUN1MG087bhY1lhajigDkZMpHyc2ImWIYEPBLC0NK75p\nexaUB8QeQMewlF9yrUhOjocBJ9g7T1A5hD5eRxkJhuYxyi3XAXf2HALNDEsSmVsB\nmlrycxJEwqPX+AGQ/LjrW4hFQjGoi0kaoVz0MRCkj9Q35Z1sLMHfKhRxjiXYyHj4\nmJQmRH6W3DU8je+D6uIf9I7uE8TcRSMi0IyF9TTNipKnDjSXHYWtFgPTEsB2RCqR\nikC4+7+9XSREB6hC7uV/V4lp9Kg3xZbuouHyvZN7WF4FuPZb6pWiML5wanmyriIk\nzOI5SUKUKurWC5f9n2FYNF5CsVAJBt2/HwSFmjwFacBIs6Ja0zXFr4qZcHrM1vBI\n+GY6uoAmeopXVZSHqTbQ\n=8NNB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T10:01:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKGVlMzY2MDY0MzVmOTgwMTIwY2JkOTRlMjZkMTg1ZTkzYmI5OGI5NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5","sha":"5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5"}],"sha":"ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/ee36606435f980120cbd94e26d185e93bb98b958"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:11Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:01:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(design-frames-service): correct pagination precision, comment authorRef, approve/reject validation, description default, and frame_ref indexing (#41)\n\nFive backend defects found by the independent acceptance suite (PR #40)\nagainst the Postgres lifecycle tier (#39):\n\n- Pagination cursors for projects/discussions/approvals (and, for\n  consistency, features-by-project) were built from\n  row.<timestamp>.toISOString(), which node-postgres truncates to\n  millisecond precision even though Postgres stores microseconds. A\n  boundary row sharing a millisecond with its neighbour could reappear\n  across pages. Fixed by selecting the ordering timestamp as text\n  (<col>::text) for the cursor and binding it back as an explicit\n  ::timestamptz in the WHERE clause.\n- POST /api/v1/features with an omitted `description` failed the\n  manifest''s own non-empty-string validation, even though openapi.yaml\n  only requires `slug`. Default an omitted description to the feature''s\n  resolved name instead of an empty string.\n- POST .../approve and .../reject never validated body shape, so a client\n  could send additionalProperties the openapi.yaml schema forbids. Both\n  now reject unknown properties with 400, mirroring routes/projects.ts.\n- POST .../comments accepted and echoed a client-supplied `authorRef`,\n  which is not part of CommentCreate''s schema and let any caller\n  impersonate any author. authorRef is now always server-derived (a\n  defined service-actor value); a richer per-user identity needs a\n  per-user auth model upstream of this single-shared-bearer-token\n  service.\n- frameRefRepo.upsertFrameRef was only ever called from\n  scripts/backfill.ts, so frame/element discussion targets were\n  unreachable via the live API. Wired into POST .../frames/:file''s\n  sibling stamp-persist route (POST .../stamp), indexing every actual\n  frame file present at that point.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"424bc0fcf48b3ab2b59fb0a59fc790b94a1eed18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/424bc0fcf48b3ab2b59fb0a59fc790b94a1eed18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 424bc0fcf48b3ab2b59fb0a59fc790b94a1eed18\nparent 33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787479271 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787479271 +0300\n\nfix(design-frames-service): correct pagination precision, comment authorRef, approve/reject validation, description default, and frame_ref indexing (#41)\n\nFive backend defects found by the independent acceptance suite (PR #40)\nagainst the Postgres lifecycle tier (#39):\n\n- Pagination cursors for projects/discussions/approvals (and, for\n  consistency, features-by-project) were built from\n  row.<timestamp>.toISOString(), which node-postgres truncates to\n  millisecond precision even though Postgres stores microseconds. A\n  boundary row sharing a millisecond with its neighbour could reappear\n  across pages. Fixed by selecting the ordering timestamp as text\n  (<col>::text) for the cursor and binding it back as an explicit\n  ::timestamptz in the WHERE clause.\n- POST /api/v1/features with an omitted `description` failed the\n  manifest''s own non-empty-string validation, even though openapi.yaml\n  only requires `slug`. Default an omitted description to the feature''s\n  resolved name instead of an empty string.\n- POST .../approve and .../reject never validated body shape, so a client\n  could send additionalProperties the openapi.yaml schema forbids. Both\n  now reject unknown properties with 400, mirroring routes/projects.ts.\n- POST .../comments accepted and echoed a client-supplied `authorRef`,\n  which is not part of CommentCreate''s schema and let any caller\n  impersonate any author. authorRef is now always server-derived (a\n  defined service-actor value); a richer per-user identity needs a\n  per-user auth model upstream of this single-shared-bearer-token\n  service.\n- frameRefRepo.upsertFrameRef was only ever called from\n  scripts/backfill.ts, so frame/element discussion targets were\n  unreachable via the live API. Wired into POST .../frames/:file''s\n  sibling stamp-persist route (POST .../stamp), indexing every actual\n  frame file present at that point.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqisTnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANd8QAE8F4Z/BapaVlAZVr/hfCVmL\nTnJ8MhYs+beXEsFEx5OvGGLiAHweHfszHM9OhDu/6/auvWV5jKZyar90GeJ6+44/\nsr1RKJ1dkjZfuJxY72ersy1Kr71nU8C+6Z74rGRzYgzqs+TT6AiydEMAwfP3x0Ys\n7QoOdsIcVvIg8YLMrSM9dCH0mf+WRCuF99UVXQ6wFeYNnyZFX6XtX/w/WRY7Dve/\nVxjTz9DHNsxMudvfSlC1uYMj+f0k8NhTeJSDVJbB/MciBtTFvXwWeYjjyChUAKz6\n3O+qdZgdRf6nP7BpfuvK74XwHCXCsEI/3NHiisgQ6WqjxsfmoOW1F7NVclT65wTS\nrMmGrz2ugwHCZvNftaEaY8guvkmDDE0LVj89U6575g0FwbkdxhpIqvroIz0g24ng\nvL1GXpFBEPy66F7685379bMZvTY2/sHfj8WfCUuYRMpoz00TX/hAd9GOyaB0EBph\npqpk7kCoFK9MnYNaJNGGUDS1a7Q217c1JMm/oDlUEiuVs2zG0rOeUsJRcApU6Xj0\nJY0xdmLuh/qrYIpHX1kN5Tx40zR2bY8oy3ouuRYP4ep4ElnmaSf2iCT9CHtOpGzD\nQ9re8V2wpv8P3X2N6Ai1LCFbrU6MCItVAtJKMLb1p5Wit0lq9alpZI93G/05FfSC\ntPwq/2therAbLAlnKHUO\n=eGAk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T10:01:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDUzOTFiZDRhMTAwYTM0YjY1MDI3OGY1YTY2ZjU4OTYyYmI2MWMzYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f","sha":"33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f"}],"sha":"5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/5391bd4a100a34b650278f5a66f58962bb61c3b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:38:37Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:38:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): a2a/mcp maintain — LiteLLM virtual key, fail-closed contract (#45)\n\n* fix(ci): a2a/mcp maintain — LiteLLM virtual key, fail-closed contract\n\nWas secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (provider key, vendor lock-in) with a \"no key ->\nskip, never red\" contract: a repo declaring an A2A/MCP surface could drift\nindefinitely unmaintained while the check sat green (same failure shape as\ngate-authz''s trailing `|| true` / gate-identifier''s never-set opt-in flag).\n\nNew contract, keyed off .fuze/manifest.json:\n  <block>.enabled not declared -> skip (no surface, that is the truth)\n  <block>.enabled true, no key  -> FAIL (a declared surface nobody can maintain)\n  <block>.enabled true, key set -> run\n\nAdds an ubuntu-latest `preflight` job (so the misconfiguration check can never\nsilently queue forever on a down self-hosted pool) ahead of the maintainer job,\nswitches to secrets.LITELLM_FUZE_KEY (LiteLLM virtual key) with ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\nset explicitly so the action routes through the gateway instead of 401ing\nagainst api.anthropic.com. Existing runs-on/allowed_bots customizations for\nthis repo are preserved.\n\nReference implementation: izzywdev/FuzeFront commit 9cf9373c. Canonical\ntemplate: izzywdev/FuzeSDLC PR #180.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: e77f8b61-5f8f-5ee2-bfed-0213b6ff5667\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f20381bb1605ed243a829c7ad178e6d69e44ec5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/1f20381bb1605ed243a829c7ad178e6d69e44ec5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f20381bb1605ed243a829c7ad178e6d69e44ec5\nparent 34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787467117 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467117 +0300\n\nfix(ci): a2a/mcp maintain — LiteLLM virtual key, fail-closed contract (#45)\n\n* fix(ci): a2a/mcp maintain — LiteLLM virtual key, fail-closed contract\n\nWas secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (provider key, vendor lock-in) with a \"no key ->\nskip, never red\" contract: a repo declaring an A2A/MCP surface could drift\nindefinitely unmaintained while the check sat green (same failure shape as\ngate-authz''s trailing `|| true` / gate-identifier''s never-set opt-in flag).\n\nNew contract, keyed off .fuze/manifest.json:\n  <block>.enabled not declared -> skip (no surface, that is the truth)\n  <block>.enabled true, no key  -> FAIL (a declared surface nobody can maintain)\n  <block>.enabled true, key set -> run\n\nAdds an ubuntu-latest `preflight` job (so the misconfiguration check can never\nsilently queue forever on a down self-hosted pool) ahead of the maintainer job,\nswitches to secrets.LITELLM_FUZE_KEY (LiteLLM virtual key) with ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\nset explicitly so the action routes through the gateway instead of 401ing\nagainst api.anthropic.com. Existing runs-on/allowed_bots customizations for\nthis repo are preserved.\n\nReference implementation: izzywdev/FuzeFront commit 9cf9373c. Canonical\ntemplate: izzywdev/FuzeSDLC PR #180.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: e77f8b61-5f8f-5ee2-bfed-0213b6ff5667\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipVtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFSoQAF6b4uJ2+Uc3qLyrBgQhzLmh\nreUavkjM6eRlzHEqg5t5OFHcgAbWD69/+OY94Kdv+oBQw5rY5flUfbyJuYbktULs\nOISBj/ekBpPmvV0i7Yr7seQG4Jc7Ol5n2BHOMr7xkK9821gJUmu/GMfrVj2rOREb\n+Cm8b1i199lt7gF6bQC1dFgNA3QgfRau1jckKBSzJa2WT5hLyyOuriCHOkKcKGUI\nfMEEue9uLF/BxGLVJlguPZlDzX7iJq0L4MIC+sLtFLjgg7E4uQl1Wdl73TYaLaW8\n1cSrVT4cyJlt4aREXVXMQFeiNyYCShYAVCRdNCEDK1hDey/OYl5tSaHdMr3bB7oN\npFIwOEBuRHb4kzjUpIXXAh+UehsbSZ33mgHppGCkqALwi2VBz+CluBizO9MjdeLe\n808ZKOXlHdiIZgHSkoNlGBAknLNmMMnElfWi91fsnOiBRy/yZqB1NPVf35Q8Ii6c\nnAj5NEuj4Ai5iMLCLS17Hq049xX7rutZZHYgcXmnqzQF5SaCn0DRp+f51MKk+moE\n+nq6ubQFaJ4q8VQJZG2bwbVnrJt0lSdEPce4BPpRQ0bFKSdgvx97Iw5L29FCBMyn\n8atcvet1ccrpmjNzaXUNURnDyv406Liv0vVlpuhrE8X8ApBQlNfHJlF+EI+7QNdQ\nKZ6hCLLTfPTViEUPT/E2\n=8jo0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:38:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDMzMjUwYzQ3NzlmMzQyMDU3ZDY4OTQ2OWU5NTk1YjFiYjgwMDM2NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649","sha":"34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649"}],"sha":"33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/33250c4779f342057d689469e9595b1bb800365f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:41:18Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:41:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deploy): flip fuzex prod release live, drop orphan imagePullSecret (#42)\n\nBoth go-live blockers documented in values-prod.yaml are now satisfied:\nthe image ghcr.io/izzywdev/fuzex-design-frames-service:6aa1c11f6aff is\npublished (verified against the GHCR manifest API), and the\nfuzefront-registration SealedSecret exists in the fuzex namespace. Flip\n`enabled: true` so Argo (once the Application is registered by FuzeInfra''s\none-time argocd-register step) creates the fuzex namespace and runs the\nDeployment/Service/PVC.\n\nAlso drop `imagePullSecrets: [{name: ghcr-pull}]` — it named a Secret that\nwas never sealed anywhere in this repo (no SealedSecret manifest, no chart\ntemplate renders one). The package is confirmed PUBLIC via an anonymous\nGHCR pull token, so no pull credential is needed; the orphan reference\nwould only have risked \"secret not found\" at pod creation for nothing.\n\ningress/federatedMount stay disabled: ingress.host needs new DNS + a\nCloudflare tunnel rule (FuzeInfra); federatedMount would reuse\nFuzeFront''s existing app.fuzefront.com host but adding a second\nnamespace''s Ingress against it is a separate, cross-repo routing\ndecision, not part of standing up the namespace + workload.\n\n\nClaude-Session-Id: e77f8b61-5f8f-5ee2-bfed-0213b6ff5667\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e16e5dd955bcae3051820191a8bda6b5f54f8e26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/e16e5dd955bcae3051820191a8bda6b5f54f8e26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/34fe1690e03bd1dc35ad5c56e750c6e7e5592649","verification":{"payload":"tree e16e5dd955bcae3051820191a8bda6b5f54f8e26\nparent e9576699add77d18567950195292c437743074fb\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787452878 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787452878 +0300\n\nfeat(deploy): flip fuzex prod release live, drop orphan imagePullSecret (#42)\n\nBoth go-live blockers documented in values-prod.yaml are now satisfied:\nthe image ghcr.io/izzywdev/fuzex-design-frames-service:6aa1c11f6aff is\npublished (verified against the GHCR manifest API), and the\nfuzefront-registration SealedSecret exists in the fuzex namespace. Flip\n`enabled: true` so Argo (once the Application is registered by FuzeInfra''s\none-time argocd-register step) creates the fuzex namespace and runs the\nDeployment/Service/PVC.\n\nAlso drop `imagePullSecrets: [{name: ghcr-pull}]` — it named a Secret that\nwas never sealed anywhere in this repo (no SealedSecret manifest, no chart\ntemplate renders one). The package is confirmed PUBLIC via an anonymous\nGHCR pull token, so no pull credential is needed; the orphan reference\nwould only have risked \"secret not found\" at pod creation for nothing.\n\ningress/federatedMount stay disabled: ingress.host needs new DNS + a\nCloudflare tunnel rule (FuzeInfra); federatedMount would reuse\nFuzeFront''s existing app.fuzefront.com host but adding a second\nnamespace''s Ingress against it is a separate, cross-repo routing\ndecision, not part of standing up the namespace + workload.\n\n\nClaude-Session-Id: e77f8b61-5f8f-5ee2-bfed-0213b6ff5667\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqil3OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9AQQABj4HHSHeTNwvYIdy+EkkNBA\nZ12oo21SXwX