"node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/0c03bd3d311f97da2b66c839d57c92f1626ccd68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:28:36Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:28:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames-service): freeze Postgres lifecycle-tier contract (v0.2.0) (#31)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): freeze Postgres lifecycle-tier contract (v0.2.0)\n\nContract-first artifacts (no implementation) for evolving design-frames-service\nto a Postgres-backed lifecycle tier. Frame CONTENT stays in git; Postgres holds\nonly lifecycle/index metadata + refs, keyed by content-stamp.\n\n- .fuze/manifest.json: reserve identity.namespace \"fxdf\" so gate-identifier\n  recognizes the fxdf_* prefixes (project/feature/flow/frame_ref/approval/\n  discussion/comment).\n- openapi.yaml -> v0.2.0 (additive, backward-compatible): /api/v1/projects CRUD\n  + /{id}/features; optional projectId reference on POST /features; append-only\n  approvals history GET; approve/reject bodies gain optional contentStamp\n  (reject now requires reason) with responses echoing the created fxdf_apr_* id\n  + stamp; discussions + threaded comments with paired polymorphic targets.\n  Every create body sets additionalProperties:false and mints ids server-side\n  (identifier-standard §1); every polymorphic ref carries its type (§2). New\n  collection GETs paginate (limit+cursor, {items,page} envelope). The entire\n  v0.1.0 /features/** frame + manifest surface is unchanged.\n- docs/postgres-tier.md: two-tier model, entity/prefix table, append-only +\n  stamp-binding invariant, content boundary (git vs Postgres; PVC->object-store\n  evolution), manifest-projection backward-compat, dual-write/backfill migration,\n  and ownership (contract-designer -> FuzeInfra @claude -> database-engineer ->\n  backend-engineer).\n\nSpectral lint: 0 errors. No SQL/handlers/Express/pg code; no runtime deps added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* fix(contract): parentId -> parentCommentId in Comment schemas (gate-identifier)\n\ngate-identifier''s POLYMORPHIC_ID_RE flags a bare `parentId` as a polymorphic\nreference needing a `parentType` sibling. A comment''s parent is ALWAYS another\ncomment (monomorphic), so per identifier-standard the correct form is to name\nthe entity: `parentCommentId` (a typed reference like userId/organizationId),\nnot to invent a redundant parentType. gate_identifier.py now passes (OK).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* fix(contract): defer identity.namespace declaration to the implementation PR\n\ngate-identifier''s --adoption check becomes ENFORCING the moment .fuze/manifest.json\ndeclares an identity block, and it then requires the repo to DEPEND on an identity\npackage (@izzywdev/fuzefront-identity) because it ships create operations — a\npackage this contract-only PR does not (and should not) add. Per identifier-standard\n9, the namespace declaration and the identity package land together in the\nbackend-engineer implementation stream. Removed the identity block here; the design\ndoc reserves the fxdf_* prefixes and the OpenAPI create bodies already satisfy the\nid-shape rules (C1/C2/C3 pass) without the namespace declaration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"07b3d8a7f274faf9738e047c57efcea5839cd7e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/07b3d8a7f274faf9738e047c57efcea5839cd7e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/0c03bd3d311f97da2b66c839d57c92f1626ccd68","verification":{"payload":"tree 07b3d8a7f274faf9738e047c57efcea5839cd7e4\nparent 2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787207316 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787207316 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames-service): freeze Postgres lifecycle-tier contract (v0.2.0) (#31)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): freeze Postgres lifecycle-tier contract (v0.2.0)\n\nContract-first artifacts (no implementation) for evolving design-frames-service\nto a Postgres-backed lifecycle tier. Frame CONTENT stays in git; Postgres holds\nonly lifecycle/index metadata + refs, keyed by content-stamp.\n\n- .fuze/manifest.json: reserve identity.namespace \"fxdf\" so gate-identifier\n  recognizes the fxdf_* prefixes (project/feature/flow/frame_ref/approval/\n  discussion/comment).\n- openapi.yaml -> v0.2.0 (additive, backward-compatible): /api/v1/projects CRUD\n  + /{id}/features; optional projectId reference on POST /features; append-only\n  approvals history GET; approve/reject bodies gain optional contentStamp\n  (reject now requires reason) with responses echoing the created fxdf_apr_* id\n  + stamp; discussions + threaded comments with paired polymorphic targets.\n  Every create body sets additionalProperties:false and mints ids server-side\n  (identifier-standard §1); every polymorphic ref carries its type (§2). New\n  collection GETs paginate (limit+cursor, {items,page} envelope). The entire\n  v0.1.0 /features/** frame + manifest surface is unchanged.\n- docs/postgres-tier.md: two-tier model, entity/prefix table, append-only +\n  stamp-binding invariant, content boundary (git vs Postgres; PVC->object-store\n  evolution), manifest-projection backward-compat, dual-write/backfill migration,\n  and ownership (contract-designer -> FuzeInfra @claude -> database-engineer ->\n  backend-engineer).\n\nSpectral lint: 0 errors. No SQL/handlers/Express/pg code; no runtime deps added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* fix(contract): parentId -> parentCommentId in Comment schemas (gate-identifier)\n\ngate-identifier''s POLYMORPHIC_ID_RE flags a bare `parentId` as a polymorphic\nreference needing a `parentType` sibling. A comment''s parent is ALWAYS another\ncomment (monomorphic), so per identifier-standard the correct form is to name\nthe entity: `parentCommentId` (a typed reference like userId/organizationId),\nnot to invent a redundant parentType. gate_identifier.py now passes (OK).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* fix(contract): defer identity.namespace declaration to the implementation PR\n\ngate-identifier''s --adoption check becomes ENFORCING the moment .fuze/manifest.json\ndeclares an identity block, and it then requires the repo to DEPEND on an identity\npackage (@izzywdev/fuzefront-identity) because it ships create operations — a\npackage this contract-only PR does not (and should not) add. Per identifier-standard\n9, the namespace declaration and the identity package land together in the\nbackend-engineer implementation stream. Removed the identity block here; the design\ndoc reserves the fxdf_* prefixes and the OpenAPI create bodies already satisfy the\nid-shape rules (C1/C2/C3 pass) without the namespace declaration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhp6UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkiEQAHagDZre2zYmtaH+f0XT7gPS\ntGtKDxLfwq1pSavAeePODjatgsX725mWy7sFUGhPrCrpqOPUyg6Z/zh2ZtUCq2CU\no1AxXkiEYVFJ9j/9vwmNNqFu8LTF3KRv9lU5O+NyygmhekgqlWZZlD6L9ozDGoJ6\nhEy7uB/UXeP8t8koiY4WGkVZDXVz0rrOTGnpuqTti9m0VwWo3h6fSGIk58pa/x3f\ng3WdK+pijVLzlrEsr6JJXBJUUIIQCen2kNAELW42Ru1TsrMSFD1HvMQNlfxV4PtK\ntCtvVkeWpJByZ/mN+nEQbA7cjKsMp/OQSXNOEzb8R7Mz3HS/FD+hQpXLxS9nquSP\n54IZjeYvaqnb9odLkQkVGjkXI9rSAwhkzPPO5t58QFf3GeHD+gTGRHqxmMefU9gj\njTUNNQvtyKR7rkJtpNzr8od6n28LJILyGyDa9WcicU7+ULqZR/80pdXufAxTlR6C\niVCsAWmWLnlvKj1TA714USChfAVeN7a31BzzlnynD1mmYrPehfEcK9YJqJ2l1bTI\n8ZbVK6LpqHSY92Q2Y7QNOGCl5wIfxwY0lHOQUBXxeDlsydef29eptM2UKp+Ru0K7\nVUHdROJ/mK9gWFkNjfVQSAEb11wuSjT3Vreqk9EWUU5w4br0tRZ/QK9Mj8gPVoqU\n8eBUToGPoThqkr4mWyeL\n=LHTH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T06:28:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/0c03bd3d311f97da2b66c839d57c92f1626ccd68","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDBjMDNiZDNkMzExZjk3ZGEyYjY2YzgzOWQ1N2M5MmYxNjI2Y2NkNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a","sha":"2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a"}],"sha":"0c03bd3d311f97da2b66c839d57c92f1626ccd68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/0c03bd3d311f97da2b66c839d57c92f1626ccd68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:53:50Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:53:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools (#33)\n\n* ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools\n\nizzywdev/AITools held only two reusable workflows and a README, and is being deleted.\nBoth now live in the canonical (FuzeSDLC#122), so the caller stubs repoint:\n\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n\nThis is only possible now because AITools was PUBLIC and FuzeSDLC is PRIVATE: a\nprivate repo''s workflows are by default callable only from that same repo. The owner\nhas opened Settings -> Actions -> General -> Access (\"Accessible from repositories\nowned by the user\"), so these resolve.\n\nNO `runner:` INPUT HERE, deliberately. The reusable workflows now take one, because a\nreusable workflow''s job runs in the CALLER''s context and bills to the CALLER -- which\non a private repo with the Actions budget exhausted means it never starts at all. This\nrepo is PUBLIC, so its GitHub-hosted jobs run unmetered and the `ubuntu-latest` default\nis correct. Passing a value would be change for its own sake.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"de269148d2411cd3aecbe8f7125b815b9a7d157e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/de269148d2411cd3aecbe8f7125b815b9a7d157e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/2351f7942c0d313317a59c5be2931e5006b2ca4a","verification":{"payload":"tree de269148d2411cd3aecbe8f7125b815b9a7d157e\nparent 858d0189b068d096efa2fab0498922b9a4a57544\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787169230 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169230 +0300\n\nci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools (#33)\n\n* ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools\n\nizzywdev/AITools held only two reusable workflows and a README, and is being deleted.\nBoth now live in the canonical (FuzeSDLC#122), so the caller stubs repoint:\n\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n\nThis is only possible now because AITools was PUBLIC and FuzeSDLC is PRIVATE: a\nprivate repo''s workflows are by default callable only from that same repo. The owner\nhas opened Settings -> Actions -> General -> Access (\"Accessible from repositories\nowned by the user\"), so these resolve.\n\nNO `runner:` INPUT HERE, deliberately. The reusable workflows now take one, because a\nreusable workflow''s job runs in the CALLER''s context and bills to the CALLER -- which\non a private repo with the Actions budget exhausted means it never starts at all. This\nrepo is PUBLIC, so its GitHub-hosted jobs run unmetered and the `ubuntu-latest` default\nis correct. Passing a value would be change for its own sake.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgnOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlA