g_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/8f28e15a50a4c13a7183abe353a025dfe57acb25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:33:55Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:33:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames): build + serve the MF remote, add same-origin portal mount (#29)\n\n* feat(design-frames): build + serve the MF remote, add same-origin portal mount\n\nMakes the design-frames Module-Federation remote (added in #27) actually\nbuild and be served, and adds the reverse-proxy mount so the FuzeFront portal\nloads it same-origin.\n\n- Dockerfile: multi-stage — node:24-alpine builder runs `vite build` on\n  webapp/ (DS from GitHub Packages via a BuildKit `--mount=type=secret`\n  GITHUB_TOKEN, never in a layer); runtime copies dist -> /app/webapp-dist\n  (ENV DESIGN_FRAMES_WEBAPP_DIR).\n- server.js: serves /apps/fuzex/* (remoteEntry.js, chunks, index.html) with\n  correct MIME types + encoded-traversal defense; reads public like /site.\n  +4 tests (17/17 pass).\n- CI: design-frames-service-ci docker-build passes the Packages token via\n  BuildKit secret + smoke-checks /apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js; release.yml gets\n  the same secret so the published image contains the built assets.\n- Helm: webapp.dir override; new default-OFF `federatedMount` Ingress\n  (templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml) that routes {host}/apps/fuzex/* to\n  this service as a pass-through — it lives here because an Ingress can only\n  target a same-namespace Service (fuzex ns), routed by the cluster Traefik.\n\nPREREQUISITE (owner, before CI can go green): the @izzywdev/fuzefront-design-system\npackage must grant izzywdev/FuzeX Actions read access, or the builder-stage\nnpm install 401s and docker-build fails. This is a package-settings action, not\na code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* ci: re-trigger gates on PR head\n\ngovernance-sync auto-committed a managed-file reconcile with [skip ci], which\norphaned the required checks on the branch head (they passed on the prior\ncommit). This empty commit re-runs them on the current head so the PR can go\ngreen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"502575edd41a01aa43281804d5ace3dc20aaa06d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/502575edd41a01aa43281804d5ace3dc20aaa06d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/8f28e15a50a4c13a7183abe353a025dfe57acb25","verification":{"payload":"tree 502575edd41a01aa43281804d5ace3dc20aaa06d\nparent 6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787157235 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787157235 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames): build + serve the MF remote, add same-origin portal mount (#29)\n\n* feat(design-frames): build + serve the MF remote, add same-origin portal mount\n\nMakes the design-frames Module-Federation remote (added in #27) actually\nbuild and be served, and adds the reverse-proxy mount so the FuzeFront portal\nloads it same-origin.\n\n- Dockerfile: multi-stage — node:24-alpine builder runs `vite build` on\n  webapp/ (DS from GitHub Packages via a BuildKit `--mount=type=secret`\n  GITHUB_TOKEN, never in a layer); runtime copies dist -> /app/webapp-dist\n  (ENV DESIGN_FRAMES_WEBAPP_DIR).\n- server.js: serves /apps/fuzex/* (remoteEntry.js, chunks, index.html) with\n  correct MIME types + encoded-traversal defense; reads public like /site.\n  +4 tests (17/17 pass).\n- CI: design-frames-service-ci docker-build passes the Packages token via\n  BuildKit secret + smoke-checks /apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js; release.yml gets\n  the same secret so the published image contains the built assets.\n- Helm: webapp.dir override; new default-OFF `federatedMount` Ingress\n  (templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml) that routes {host}/apps/fuzex/* to\n  this service as a pass-through — it lives here because an Ingress can only\n  target a same-namespace Service (fuzex ns), routed by the cluster Traefik.\n\nPREREQUISITE (owner, before CI can go green): the @izzywdev/fuzefront-design-system\npackage must grant izzywdev/FuzeX Actions read access, or the builder-stage\nnpm install 401s and docker-build fails. This is a package-settings action, not\na code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* ci: re-trigger gates on PR head\n\ngovernance-sync auto-committed a managed-file reconcile with [skip ci], which\norphaned the required checks on the branch head (they passed on the prior\ncommit). This empty commit re-runs them on the current head so the PR can go\ngreen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhdrzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi70QAGPYtDRRSOEVg/ZV3X+T/JIR\nlR2n7ULOSquO/nr7rgxtG27bZrfgT2u0oBFLcWrMaiHa8qzSjGRii4vSH8e3JlNZ\nki+PiRZqy2ncvnIxq213mLx4EWEqCc1XI+nn77C4lu5SiP26HLWUQV4vJSRuzwDV\nd/5rWh7KBS4YZ818MtPKFQgBepXxG3+wzj8ywKVAd1PmPaYVTASwBbV8QnYzsSMr\nC47/kDSWtGnYuF0PinNK6u2rmtKd0KCLeex5Sg/+SmOtxnj2ys9AgQg5jEgRyq0h\nMJ4FYUQcvAlyKBTiEYbpe7zJrAfltYY5l7S0dcDXzVfjq+3AfSVsIQ2UtJUniUxE\nJQnNK/DzevdllB4KxOKltQSIO5bJsX8MhOQt0zc2GWJGVySdBwbuWYwlt6UfFzw0\nZUFOCXzAXzKQOZNviAP6Ri27MeU0+QdvR6RlOYL33rPXE2cz4lSSegUFJULmxzVi\n7zchYLFkxcWUo0zLamtteYw/aLh1hLD55HS+SxYPrS8nJEKltQ1enpQ5xsY2IGd+\ng2qFuEcXwv5PSYHRfiTmTBAvpec/zfCcIfFudQrCAVQuhx+sHpGk8rdZtJSslURg\n3ARKyKXU3lHDGQNkgR9i9vcDDY9+J67t/XJd51DFiQifShDRPWfXlVGbPJL/wXMs\nGKHWC1pUZntO6bq3VT92\n=EEEW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T16:33:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/8f28e15a50a4c13a7183abe353a025dfe57acb25","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKDhmMjhlMTVhNTBhNGMxM2E3MTgzYWJlMzUzYTAyNWRmZTU3YWNiMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa","sha":"6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa"}],"sha":"8f28e15a50a4c13a7183abe353a025dfe57acb25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/8f28e15a50a4c13a7183abe353a025dfe57acb25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T12:57:14Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T12:57:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.6.0 — capability installer, wave 2 (#28)\n\n* chore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.6.0 — capability installer, wave 2\n\nWave-2 rollout. FuzeX and FuzeKeys exercise the one defect wave 1 could not\nreach: origin/HEAD is UNSET here, and this repo defaults to master, not main.\n\nThe old shell died silently on exactly this. ''git symbolic-ref'' exits 1 when\norigin/HEAD is unset, and under ''set -e'' + ''pipefail'' that killed the script\nBEFORE the banner printed, making the fallbacks on the next two lines\nunreachable. The guarded rung chain resolves it and says which rung answered:\n\n    bootstrap izzywdev/FuzeX (baselineRef=v1, branch=master via remote show)\n\n9 workflows now render ''branches: [master]''. Stamped [main] they would never\nfire, and a workflow that never fires reports nothing — not failure.\n\nFOUND WHILE VERIFYING THAT, and fixed here: .github/workflows/gate-registration.yml\nhad ''push: branches: [main]'' — and this repo has NO main branch at all, so that\npush trigger has never once fired in its life. It is repo-local, so the\ninstaller does not own it and left it alone; the one-line fix is included\nbecause it is the same class of defect this rollout exists to find. Its\npull_request trigger was unaffected and did work.\n\nportal.registers is false here and the opt-out is honoured — portal-registration\nplanned nothing. The pre-existing registration/ payload is untouched.\n\nmf-remote is a no-op: this repo''s design-frames remote already declares\nreact/react-dom as { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^19.0.0'' }, so there is\nno bare-array rewrite here and none of the ''Invalid hook call'' risk that keeps\nthe four array-shaped repos gated.\n\n77 files, including 16 stale governance files adopted with --adopt-canonical\n(FuzeSDLC#95). No self-hosted runners and no genuine local customization lost.\n\nVerified idempotent: a second run writes 0 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(api): POST /api/v1/features rejects undeclared fields (gate-identifier)\n\ngate-identifier landed with this bootstrap and flagged the feature-create body\nfor not setting additionalProperties: false — the OWASP API3:2023\nmass-assignment surface identifier-standard.md 1 exists to close. Without it a\nclient can post fields the schema does not declare, including an id for a\nresource the service is supposed to mint.\n\nUnlike FuzeKeys, this spec is hand-authored — no generator header, no exporter\nscript — so the schema IS the source of truth and editing it here is the fix\nrather than something a regeneration would revert.\n\nBEHAVIOUR CHANGE: a create request carrying an undeclared field is now a\nvalidation error instead of having the field silently ignored.\n\nVerified: gate_identifier.py exits 0 against this repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(sdlc): adopt hardened workflow templates (FuzeSDLC#98)\n\nPicks up three canonical fixes that wave 2 itself surfaced:\n\n  * publish-expert.yml HAD NEVER PARSED — two python heredocs at column 0\n    terminated the enclosing ''run: |'' block, so YAML read them as mapping keys.\n    This repo has carried a workflow that could never run, reporting nothing.\n  * claude.yml no longer interpolates github-context data into a shell.\n    A branch name may contain '';'', ''|'', ''$'' and backticks, so the old\n    HEAD_REF=\"\\${{ ... head.ref }}\" was a runner-side script injection.\n    Every context value now arrives via env: and is referenced quoted.\n  * 48 action references pinned to 40-char commit SHAs (tags can be repointed\n    by their owner — the trivy-action / kics-github-action attack).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0730fd51a49a02218b1f13a0f70b657c2ad66538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/0730fd51a49a02218b1f13a0f70b657c2ad66538"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/6006b303200c32e5c293425caeee7cc6d0285faa","verification":{"payload":"tree 0730fd51a49a02218b1f13a0f70b657c2ad66538\nparent c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787057834 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787057834 +0300\n\nchore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.6.0 — capability installer, wave 2 (#28)\n\n* chore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.6.0 — capability installer, wave 2\n\nWave-2 rollout. FuzeX and FuzeKeys exercise the one defect wave 1 could not\nreach: origin/HEAD is UNSET here, and this repo defaults to master, not main.\n\nThe old shell died silently on exactly this. ''git symbolic-ref'' exits 1 when\norigin/HEAD is unset, and under ''set -e'' + ''pipefail'' that killed the script\nBEFORE the banner printed, making the fallbacks on the next two lines\nunreachable. The guarded rung chain resolves it and says which rung answered:\n\n    bootstrap izzywdev/FuzeX (baselineRef=v1, branch=master via remote show)\n\n9 workflows now render ''branches: [master]''. Stamped [main] they would never\nfire, and a workflow that never fires reports nothing — not failure.\n\nFOUND WHILE VERIFYING THAT, and fixed here: .github/workflows/gate-registration.yml\nhad ''push: branches: [main]'' — and this repo has NO main branch at all, so that\npush trigger has never once fired in its life. It is repo-local, so the\ninstaller does not own it and left it alone; the one-line fix is included\nbecause it is the same class of defect this rollout exists to find. Its\npull_request trigger was unaffected and did work.\n\nportal.registers is false here and the opt-out is honoured — portal-registration\nplanned nothing. The pre-existing registration/ payload is untouched.\n\nmf-remote is a no-op: this repo''s design-frames remote already declares\nreact/react-dom as { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^19.0.0'' }, so there is\nno bare-array rewrite here and none of the ''Invalid hook call'' risk that keeps\nthe four array-shaped repos gated.\n\n77 files, including 16 stale governance files adopted with --adopt-canonical\n(FuzeSDLC#95). No self-hosted runners and no genuine local customization lost.\n\nVerified idempotent: a second run writes 0 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(api): POST /api/v1/features rejects undeclared fields (gate-identifier)\n\ngate-identifier landed with this bootstrap and flagged the feature-create body\nfor not setting additionalProperties: false — the OWASP API3:2023\nmass-assignment surface identifier-standard.md 1 exists to close. Without it a\nclient can post fields the schema does not declare, including an id for a\nresource the service is supposed to mint.\n\nUnlike FuzeKeys, this spec is hand-authored — no generator header, no exporter\nscript — so the schema IS the source of truth and editing it here is the fix\nrather than something a regeneration would revert.\n\nBEHAVIOUR CHANGE: a create request carrying an undeclared field is now a\nvalidation error instead of having the field silently ignored.\n\nVerified: gate_identifier.py exits 0 against this repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(sdlc): adopt hardened workflow templates (FuzeSDLC#98)\n\nPicks up three canonical fixes that wave 2 itself surfaced:\n\n  * publish-expert.yml HAD NEVER PARSED — two python heredocs at column 0\n    terminated the enclosing ''run: |'' block, so YAML read them as mapping keys.\n    This repo has carried a workflow that could never run, reporting nothing.\n  * claude.yml no longer interpolates github-context data into a shell.\n    A branch name may contain '';'', ''|'', ''$'' and backticks, so the old\n    HEAD_REF=\"\\${{ ... head.ref }}\" was a runner-side script injection.\n    Every context value now arrives via env: and is referenced quoted.\n  * 48 action references pinned to 40-char commit SHAs (tags can be repointed\n    by their owner — the trivy-action / kics-github-action attack).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhFaqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADBMQAHdPirJqa9xI26+uEp34sQdk\nZmKOumqtQxg1ihrTpi0BFWwAYbY6W3X4UaycnFwk1mE7PpUjRewtS0cmZ1/GsBR+\n8mELvne3qHJDSjmxM/GcbBtzYM+iE/VkUpEXFOdpiGSOIuPbDoFml6cIMoxx2XY1\ng+givfvTh/H7mZ/hxLObz0pjxcih2u1TBrKVgsV1Uj6VLOsHu1w2i+Y80FfRx9MN\nR7sutWTKbJFOW+otPHetL4wmnqRCHAYxxDnZjXg/TcyOb8nG1RwKZjHe1bU6z3mh\nmgyQtMh5dG+wgSn/zzuwQflTEjrGZbDEwNQGPC/EVxerFUtZWj5N2+IwvfbMBbNA\nE4cYmXX4DBgMs95k9IQdFqv6+XmCY/w6YubdOYO1IZHNFe9YqOMIOl6ysCqJ/W+8\nZkmbmMCpBJxMdJ4ePUTAVGv5a1Jrn5mTIaTLz/kt6L1q76IstClBz6GYJGgvyciZ\nlXbxXJ2pbIY/atagyhfT7ZrKyJrDOVLlSXkm+RRQtyuqxSr6iSvvfuCsmkWijFm7\nNFvmpESeV8dGDDyAS4ETOWM5cAbVIIOsuxIN274ZVE1Sog0/g4nQ6FdwhdfwuTw/\nGJ8ZF760vAHLPVaamCww5Br4UXKjwO4sa9RPVCHtYV2VfcA8xlfZnlN53DNFO1LW\n1tm4x8VN3zqJe84VznMR\n=OQel\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_