in":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T11:54:52Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T11:54:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames): React Module-Federation remote for FuzeFront portal embedding (#27)\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service/webapp — a Vite + @vitejs/plugin-react +\n@originjs/vite-plugin-federation remote that reproduces the design-frames review\nUI in React on @izzywdev/fuzefront-design-system, so it mounts as an embedded\nmicro-frontend in the FuzeFront portal shell (shared React 19 singleton), NOT an\niframe. Federation: scope \"fuzex\", exposes ./DesignFramesApp, react/react-dom\nshared singletons ^19.0.0, base /apps/fuzex/ (remoteEntry.js at that path).\n\n- webapp/: base-path-aware REST client (window.DESIGN_FRAMES_API_BASE), feature\n  list / frame viewer / per-flow approve+reject with real loading/empty/error\n  states, DS components only (no raw hex/px).\n- registration/manifest.json (+ vendored helm copy, byte-identical): integration\n  flips spa -> module-federation (remoteEntry /apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js, scope\n  fuzex, module ./DesignFramesApp).\n- .fuze/manifest.json: portal.registers true; reason updated for the MF remote.\n\nBackend/service, Dockerfile build+serve of the remote, the host reverse-proxy for\n/apps/fuzex/, the app-registry schema relax (accept same-origin relative\nremoteEntry), and registration+activation are follow-ups (devops / FuzeFront /\nFuzeInfra). Remote build verified locally (vite build emits remoteEntry.js).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea867dd0fdb2df9023cf5469d0581537d276d472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/ea867dd0fdb2df9023cf5469d0581537d276d472"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df","verification":{"payload":"tree ea867dd0fdb2df9023cf5469d0581537d276d472\nparent dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787054092 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787054092 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames): React Module-Federation remote for FuzeFront portal embedding (#27)\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service/webapp — a Vite + @vitejs/plugin-react +\n@originjs/vite-plugin-federation remote that reproduces the design-frames review\nUI in React on @izzywdev/fuzefront-design-system, so it mounts as an embedded\nmicro-frontend in the FuzeFront portal shell (shared React 19 singleton), NOT an\niframe. Federation: scope \"fuzex\", exposes ./DesignFramesApp, react/react-dom\nshared singletons ^19.0.0, base /apps/fuzex/ (remoteEntry.js at that path).\n\n- webapp/: base-path-aware REST client (window.DESIGN_FRAMES_API_BASE), feature\n  list / frame viewer / per-flow approve+reject with real loading/empty/error\n  states, DS components only (no raw hex/px).\n- registration/manifest.json (+ vendored helm copy, byte-identical): integration\n  flips spa -> module-federation (remoteEntry /apps/fuzex/remoteEntry.js, scope\n  fuzex, module ./DesignFramesApp).\n- .fuze/manifest.json: portal.registers true; reason updated for the MF remote.\n\nBackend/service, Dockerfile build+serve of the remote, the host reverse-proxy for\n/apps/fuzex/, the app-registry schema relax (accept same-origin relative\nremoteEntry), and registration+activation are follow-ups (devops / FuzeFront /\nFuzeInfra). Remote build verified locally (vite build emits remoteEntry.js).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhEgMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlMAQAA4CU98qzEEQIr96fyzeOu4l\n26OvyIeU5IAG8GDiIj7h1dcOo2v3dXY/bIZ89R4PvZiMpym0CXZqIji2E68F6aVE\n4CIKMBPxMKFRu/FBwltym31Y6AFvJmDDwFuaruRofGJ/2TVGVdHlIgudQWHLwxJd\nr4+p7C6EzSOEeWyOTE/Ujmu2v+f2dDkHUmu2fGGsNYt307NGsWtmReyuRfoFjnCc\nq9JOaQixUYdPtlTPJ1aDjy0ma81Ozc/FSmxP76/AK+OJijghB5EdjcTp4kPWeju5\nu+thpdC/i0Nzic0a/gDWPie5m9SLq529uqBb5/oI+gKlo/VReGKjVDwYVVb4VQa3\nKiFniSJi7ez/+Y0C1Z6Y2SSpQtAYCjc/KwVQsay3qUNu3MeV7cbFX/TbkVwj9dIj\nUdxYd5peiMQ42CvFmgB7Tsw0WY1J1sSYGDe9fjCxeb4zVENZ+uyaDXQYWAcW8Hzo\nl6aMzKPUPofCjJ854nzqioaN8V9zMT5iNxYZBDEEIb8PWw4CkPdpPyuwEkrsqPml\nimWHY7XjlooZnZFcq5FAvSPM3p/wK6e6SjBOq1SXklLxRhTvLMdg3PuYjoNEW1c9\nuTidouyisBma4Pz0qRT7LdzrN7X/mE5gp/lecwgXLIgxQIsqqoGepHo2bnSRBsSh\nAcFKF/nZEEJAPMp3pXcA\n=Ofdx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T11:54:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKGM3MDliZTc3OWUxYzVmOTYzZDAxN2VmOGI5OTM2Y2I2Y2YzNTI3ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11","sha":"dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11"}],"sha":"c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/c709be779e1c5f963d017ef8b9936cb6cf3527df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:10:00Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:10:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(design-frames-service): frames stay in the owning repo; FuzeX owns lifecycle, not storage (#22)\n\n* fix(design-frames-service): frames stay in the owning repo; FuzeX owns lifecycle, not storage\n\nThe initial extraction (PR #21) read as \"new features author frames in FuzeX\ninstead of their own repo.\" That''s wrong — frames are data, like a .fig file:\nauthored and version-controlled in whichever product repo owns the feature,\nnever inside this repo. design-frames-service manages their LIFECYCLE (per-flow\napproval/reject, a navigable review site), not their storage or authorship.\n\n- Add the installable client package (client/design-frames-client.mjs) with a\n  new `sync` command: publish a locally-authored design/frames/<feature>/\n  directory here (create-if-missing, push frames, push manifest, commit stamp).\n  Previously only list/get/stamp/approve existed on FuzeFront''s copy of this\n  client — no create/putManifest/putFrame/commitStamp/reject, so there was no\n  way to actually publish local content here.\n- Add the canonical design-frames-lifecycle skill\n  (services/design-frames-service/skills/design-frames-lifecycle/SKILL.md)\n  documenting the corrected procedure for any consuming repo to install.\n- Correct README.md and docs/EXTRACTION.md to describe ingestion of\n  locally-authored content instead of authorship moving here.\n\nCompanion PR on izzywdev/FuzeFront removes gate-frames-external (which blocked\nnew local design/frames/<feature>/ directories) and restores local authorship\nas the policy for all features, installing this skill for the sync step.\n\n* chore(governance): add agent-templates framework scaffolding from FuzeSDLC v1\n\nAdds the four framework subtrees (schema, roles/_base, sync, providers)\nthat governance_sync.py''s FRAMEWORK_DIRS requires once an agent-templates/\ndirectory exists in the repo (created here by the a2a design-review role).\nCopied byte-exact from the FuzeSDLC canonical at baselineRef v1. Clears the\nblocking governance-sync failure (missing=4 -> 0); repo-owned\nroles/design-review/ is untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d26cd10fd83ce6619adf51f2b6c5041c85962a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/6d26cd10fd83ce6619adf51f2b6c5041c85962a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/dad95d6ee5ca8ef56c3a6ecc3b6767840e4fec11","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d26cd10fd83ce6619adf51f2b6c5041c85962a1\nparent e78f0bf939b67149d9baf27e6ea590a74449b0d1\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1786885800 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786885800 +0300\n\nfix(design-frames-service): frames stay in the owning repo; FuzeX owns lifecycle, not storage (#22)\n\n* fix(design-frames-service): frames stay in the owning repo; FuzeX owns lifecycle, not storage\n\nThe initial extraction (PR #21) read as \"new features author frames in FuzeX\ninstead of their own repo.\" That''s wrong — frames are data, like a .fig file:\nauthored and version-controlled in whichever product repo owns the feature,\nnever inside this repo. design-frames-service manages their LIFECYCLE (per-flow\napproval/reject, a navigable review site), not their storage or authorship.\n\n- Add the installable client package (client/design-frames-client.mjs) with a\n  new `sync` command: publish a locally-authored design/frames/<feature>/\n  directory here (create-if-missing, push frames, push manifest, commit stamp).\n  Previously only list/get/stamp/approve existed on FuzeFront''s copy of this\n  client — no create/putManifest/putFrame/commitStamp/reject, so there was no\n  way to actually publish local content here.\n- Add the canonical design-frames-lifecycle skill\n  (services/design-frames-service/skills/design-frames-lifecycle/SKILL.md)\n  documenting the corrected procedure for any consuming repo to install.\n- Correct README.md and docs/EXTRACTION.md to describe ingestion of\n  locally-authored content instead of authorship moving here.\n\nCompanion PR on izzywdev/FuzeFront removes gate-frames-external (which blocked\nnew local design/frames/<feature>/ directories) and restores local authorship\nas the policy for all features, installing this skill for the sync step.\n\n* chore(governance): add agent-templates framework scaffolding from FuzeSDLC v1\n\nAdds the four framework subtrees (schema, roles/_base, sync, providers)\nthat governance_sync.py''s FRAMEWORK_DIRS requires once an agent-templates/\ndirectory exists in the repo (created here by the a2a design-review role).\nCopied byte-exact from the FuzeSDLC canonical at baselineRef v1. Clears the\nblocking governance-sync failure (missing=4 -> 0); repo-owned\nroles/design-review/ is untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qg8KtEiKTkK5CTL6eKLjDy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgbaoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvQAQAKFV8PBaLwdlrivn51iMENl1\napbZ2muPdTuM+YU2kK2kgQ/YL6LPR92xFXTGWyEj5YRF6GBfOE1y3QLvDMkh1wIK\nnTbEDEuDK2z1r6ZhTZYRssWrfYBHO1O/Q9XVVTWkkLkzd74iVblW5vFRDMel/OkW\nwB28Kffop2tGQD4YWwTpZD4nqcz9q6kgmfMkoahElxhKEXw6q13I7j7swK3hEny1\nW7RsSSFWfPX6Bqd4F4JOkZPO3BPRyw5tExZgOZMeL4HdOJJ8w8cqIzhbKyl4+6GS\nRupNFfGX2krYQgApvblVgXExxfNZJ0ihn5rwi2Kl0G2RoyZ3xL6lDxQVQALF8Uk/\nHHG71+usHgjPp9XV1r4APrK/G+Xqy1KhrJPHug6bWiQFHeDpES8DOOneqGuIFQr9\njj7sZdxKZAu8n8/K81fE+zkDwL9cozzTvMDD4feHsr/ynx/D3njNP0YGI+ojva/B\nbOfQse7zGlAc5J/r5FcKw7AhKrb83MjeZqP3GMrVFuwjthHgqSkuClJTBa+POuK0\nKgNjZLxdJLmntlZRBH5Nf8396BQOrN+Uq+uQ0A++ajJyg2AJRg4cOWw7oAHoPW0I\nNZcwxyh9Iov3BRGTtcjL