"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:12:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design-frames-service): extract FuzeFront''s navigable-frames pipeline into a standalone product (#21)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): extract FuzeFront''s navigable-frames pipeline into a standalone product\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service — a REST/MCP/A2A-consumable product-design\nservice that ports the concepts behind FuzeFront''s design/frames/** pipeline\n(content-stamped navigable HTML frames, per-flow approval, a build-inventory\ncontract seam) into its own network-reachable service in this repo, rather\nthan living as files + CI glue inside FuzeFront itself.\n\n- REST API (server.js, plain node:http, no framework — matches bridge-server.js''s\n  style) + a vanilla JS/HTML frontend for browsing frames and approving flows.\n- lib/stamp.js + lib/schema.js + lib/manifest.schema.json reimplement\n  FuzeFront''s stamp-frames.mjs algorithm and manifest schema, adapted for\n  incremental (create-then-fill) authorship over an API instead of\n  whole-feature file authorship.\n- mcp/server.js + mcp/tools.json expose the same operations as MCP tools\n  (list/get/propose_frame/compute_stamp/commit_stamp/approve_flow/...).\n- agent-templates/roles/design-review/role.json is this repo''s first A2A\n  serving role; .fuze/manifest.json gains the a2a block, a second mcp.servers\n  entry, and providesTo: [FuzeFront].\n- Dockerfile + a dedicated CI workflow (test + docker build/health smoke).\n- docs/EXTRACTION.md records what was ported vs. reimplemented vs. deferred\n  (no FuzeInfra/Postgres wiring, no MF embed, FuzeFront''s 14 existing\n  features are untouched — this is plumbing for NEW features going forward).\n\nFull test suite (stamp/schema/store/server/mcp) passes: 11+ assertions green.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* chore: trigger CI on PR #21 head\n\nThe previous governance-sync commit was pushed with [skip ci], which\nprevented required checks (CI, Harden Gate, Design Frames Service CI,\ngate-line-endings, MCP Maintain) from ever running on that SHA, leaving\nthe PR permanently blocked. This empty commit re-triggers them.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"915b425ea8e887a26375ab5eba3b591be56b4e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/trees/915b425ea8e887a26375ab5eba3b591be56b4e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/git/commits/bfa3c3ecc213d6ef3034db503b2aebc193663699","verification":{"payload":"tree 915b425ea8e887a26375ab5eba3b591be56b4e89\nparent e4bea53f372e28869c122df0a0b43ffd4a8e171c\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1786381922 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786381922 +0300\n\nfeat(design-frames-service): extract FuzeFront''s navigable-frames pipeline into a standalone product (#21)\n\n* feat(design-frames-service): extract FuzeFront''s navigable-frames pipeline into a standalone product\n\nAdds services/design-frames-service — a REST/MCP/A2A-consumable product-design\nservice that ports the concepts behind FuzeFront''s design/frames/** pipeline\n(content-stamped navigable HTML frames, per-flow approval, a build-inventory\ncontract seam) into its own network-reachable service in this repo, rather\nthan living as files + CI glue inside FuzeFront itself.\n\n- REST API (server.js, plain node:http, no framework — matches bridge-server.js''s\n  style) + a vanilla JS/HTML frontend for browsing frames and approving flows.\n- lib/stamp.js + lib/schema.js + lib/manifest.schema.json reimplement\n  FuzeFront''s stamp-frames.mjs algorithm and manifest schema, adapted for\n  incremental (create-then-fill) authorship over an API instead of\n  whole-feature file authorship.\n- mcp/server.js + mcp/tools.json expose the same operations as MCP tools\n  (list/get/propose_frame/compute_stamp/commit_stamp/approve_flow/...).\n- agent-templates/roles/design-review/role.json is this repo''s first A2A\n  serving role; .fuze/manifest.json gains the a2a block, a second mcp.servers\n  entry, and providesTo: [FuzeFront].\n- Dockerfile + a dedicated CI workflow (test + docker build/health smoke).\n- docs/EXTRACTION.md records what was ported vs. reimplemented vs. deferred\n  (no FuzeInfra/Postgres wiring, no MF embed, FuzeFront''s 14 existing\n  features are untouched — this is plumbing for NEW features going forward).\n\nFull test suite (stamp/schema/store/server/mcp) passes: 11+ assertions green.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* chore: trigger CI on PR #21 head\n\nThe previous governance-sync commit was pushed with [skip ci], which\nprevented required checks (CI, Harden Gate, Design Frames Service CI,\ngate-line-endings, MCP Maintain) from ever running on that SHA, leaving\nthe PR permanently blocked. This empty commit re-triggers them.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqegZiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATOoQAIgyxN/7ciraA+07a0go11kU\n21KayiO5GvGzP8TkcZMt2xprILzfYTloki2BoDsH7edO3Cvd+AxiEZVcnoIHrYg/\nCaNxGV2EMKcX42fEz1pWFR/9etQkRBQYaqAfzBn47HfqTQ5MDwQ96MVQXgTJdVxm\nr1qPHeqppo2DvH5ZdgpZpVDCjevowrbxFzo5I+BWUAWVRtl/yqpF0xuxwTgLx0go\n3KwJXfKyGAn0hCOG1lKdAMwHg91sQpEbBRKLuY9oVk8xn785yTrC4gK4wQZEQHKl\npUdroNBDrKc+vQXDMflRsUtGgXx5sudGs28iqiV0t7thiFnIs0gN/DF2JmjC1wT3\nhqCryFUUTJYfioQsm6+LAU087wApYTHgh1rD88pM9xxLoop9moVPVgWkNo1fpAAu\nYeE7pgquWD0qbhMPzkiO6ikyCO4BqzbOquq/bwdXMhuiGJxdwho5KNwIt4QRId0f\n7yvO5Q1P+4wk2OlE3VLSftbrNSXM9KgByO2tEfyUGsOL5bDf12lD1yecj0sZ8/Em\nN0DjO3MjYfv4qQHEBxogrPkMMphdNvEirwboBZKiFWjrYAKUesbvtUSJ8mb8qKzD\n0y1kfy0I2IrtUGYqXuC0BAnZ34+5H7PHfXoUQAc8OH6ZhmY3GpV68MYZIcTsBn0W\n/8Kq2vGEiPiD8ik0Rq0P\n=dRKD\