2e28869c122df0a0b43ffd4a8e171c","node_id":"C_kwDOO8VI2toAKGU0YmVhNTNmMzcyZTI4ODY5YzEyMmRmMGEwYjQzZmZkNGE4ZTE3MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeX/commit/190fa3dd8229e80dab8689e0c0fba6a7f95fa182","sha":"190fa3dd8229e80dab8689e0c0fba6a7f95fa182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/190fa3dd8229e80dab8689e0c0fba6a7f95fa182"}],"sha":"e4bea53f372e28869c122df0a0b43ffd4a8e171c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/e4bea53f372e28869c122df0a0b43ffd4a8e171c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeX/commits/190fa3dd8229e80dab8689e0c0fba6a7f95fa182/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T09:57:07Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T09:57:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(fuze): declare FuzeX''s MCP surface; record why it does NOT register with the portal (#19)\n\n* chore(fuze): declare FuzeX''s MCP surface; record why it does NOT register with the portal\n\nFuzeX was in scope for the family-wide FuzeFront app-registration rollout. It should\nnot be: it is a Figma/FigJam PLUGIN, not a web app.\n\n  manifest.json -> editorType: [\"figma\", \"figjam\"], main: code.js, ui: ui.html\n  networkAccess -> allowedDomains restricted to localhost/127.0.0.1 (deliberate, per\n                   the comment there: wildcard ''*'' removed as a security fix)\n\nIts UI runs inside Figma''s plugin sandbox. There is no served origin to iframe and no\nremoteEntry to federate, so a portal registration would add a side-menu entry that\ncannot mount anything. Recorded as an explicit `portal.registers: false` + reason\nrather than silently skipping the repo, so the next pass over the family doesn''t\nrediscover this and \"fix\" it by adding a broken entry.\n\nWhat DOES apply here is MCP — this repo IS an MCP bridge. Declares mcp.enabled:true\nagainst bridge-server.js and adds mcp-maintainer to the agent set. Two real gaps\nflagged for that agent rather than guessed at:\n\n  1. No tools.json. The message kinds in code.js (start-server/stop-server/\n     mcp-request/client-connect/client-disconnect/get-server-status/ping) are the\n     plugin<->bridge TRANSPORT, not a tool manifest, so there is nothing yet\n     declaring the actual tool surface or which tools mutate a Figma document.\n  2. mcp-server-config.json hardcodes an absolute Windows cwd\n     (C:/Users/izzyw/source/FuzeX), so the config cannot work on another machine\n     or in CI. Left as-is: fixing it is a behaviour change, not manifest upkeep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* ci: give auto-merge.yml the write permissions it needs\n\nAuto Merge PR failed on this PR with:\n\n  GraphQL: Resource not accessible by integration (enablePullRequestAutoMerge)\n\nThe default GITHUB_TOKEN is read-only, so `gh pr merge --auto` cannot enable\nauto-merge. This is the canonical gap fixed in FuzeSDLC#66 (merged); porting the block\nhere directly rather than waiting for governance-sync to propagate it, so this PR can\nactually reach green.\n\nThe block is byte-identical to the canonical template, so the next governance-sync run\nreconciles to the same content rather than conflicting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(governance): supply the mcp-maintainer agent file + auto-merge permissions\n\nTwo red checks with the same root shape: something was DECLARED without the file\nthat backs it, and neither gate could self-heal.\n\ngovernance-sync: the manifest declares `mcp-maintainer`, and FuzeSDLC now carries\nthe canonical agent — but governance_sync.py only COPIES a file that already exists\nand has drifted. A wholly absent one is reported `missing` and hard-fails\n(governance_sync.py:84), so `--write` was never going to create it. Added\n.claude/agents/mcp-maintainer.md from the canonical, plus the mcp-maintain.yml\nworkflow where absent, so the declared surface actually has something behind it.\n\nauto-merge.yml: no permissions block, so the default read-only GITHUB_TOKEN made\n`gh pr merge --auto` fail with \"Resource not accessible by integration\" every run.\nFuzeSDLC#66 fixed the canonical template; this copy was stale. Workflow drift is\ndeliberately ADVISORY in governance-sync (the job cannot push workflow files), so\nnothing would ever have reconciled it on its own.\n\nVerified with governance_sync.py against the canonical: ok=True, missing=[].\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c542eaf0